{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_85","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"git diff --check && git status --short && sed -n '1,28p' implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":" M cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\n?? implementation_notes.md\n# Implementation notes\n\nFetch now adds the 18 word-address bits below the 1 MiB boundary. The low carry minus the offset sign selects the original, incremented, or decremented page for the full 32-bit B/J target. `PC+4` uses the same split and shares the incremented page. The halfword alignment check still qualifies prediction. [Fetch RTL](cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv)\n\nThe window check factors the three original-page comparisons into an upper-eleven-bit match and a separate low-bit match. This gives the same page-zero result for pages `0`, `1`, and `0xfff`, including 32-bit wraparound. The factored implementation gave the best measured median in the local Gowin trials. The fetch direction lookup and pending-update comparison use the XOR hash of the selected PC. Each PC candidate is hashed before applying the existing address masks.\n\nThe directed test checks long JALs in both directions, an aligned backward branch from the last mapped word, and an untaken branch with a trained taken counter whose target is `0x00100000`. It checks the request sequence through a stalled recovery, as well as retirement order, successor PCs, and link values. The test passed on both the original and revised RTL and failed with the prediction range gate disabled in a scratch copy. [Pipeline test](cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py)\n\n## Verification\n\n- Verilator lint passed without warnings. All seven cocotb runners passed.\n- A combinational SAT check proved target, range, `PC+4`, and fetch hash equivalence for word-aligned requests and mutually exclusive address masks.\n- The final single-retire ALTOPS formal run passed all 53 checks on its first attempt.\n- Co-simulation passed for selftest and three random ISS traces with ready and stalled buses. Stalled CoreMark passed all canonical CRC checks and reached the stop marker after 3,956,104 timed cycles. The local cosim and FPGA Make targets used `NRET=1`, matching `core.yaml`.\n- Gowin reported 77.271, 79.858, and 79.858 MHz and 4,091 logic cells at placement option 0. The median delivered 201.86 CoreMark iter/s, 4.69% above the champion. The low-word multiply was the longest reported path. The median clears the stated floor by about 0.07 MHz. The scratch result in the hypothesis was 83.632 MHz.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_86","type":"agent_message","text":"[Implementation notes](/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_2-sol_xhigh-v2-rep4/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261121-001-r7s0/implementation_notes.md)\n\n- Lint, cocotb, co-simulation, and all 53 formal checks passed.\n- CoreMark reached **201.86 iter/s**, up **4.69%**, in **3,956,104 timed cycles**.\n- The factored page check reached **79.858 MHz** median, above the **79.79 MHz** acceptance floor. The hypothesis scratch build reported **83.632 MHz**."}}
