ndepends on. Keep the bypass local to the branch equality comparator.\\nCompare the raw memory word with the other forwarded operand in parallel\\nby access width. For a byte or halfword, check the other operand's upper\\nbits against the required sign or zero extension of its own low bits.\\nIn parallel, compare those low bits with the raw memory lanes, then use\\nt\n…[25227 of 28299 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:081391e26facdde9]…\n \"delta_pct\": 0.68, \"vs_baseline\": 1869.88, \"fmax_mhz\": 84.986, \"ipc_coremark\": 3e-06, \"cycles\": 3559610, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 6171, \"ff\": 2769, \"seeds\": [83.197, 84.986, 84.986], \"perturbations\": [[0, 83.197, 12], [1, 84.986, 13], [2, 84.986, 13]], \"lutram\": 40, \"bsram\": 9, \"dsp\": 9, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_ex/reg_q.effective_addr_9_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_if/even_valid_q_s1\", \"slack_ns\": -7.02, \"arrival_ns\": 17.314, \"logic_cells\": 14, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_if\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 12, \"formal_passed\": true, \"cosim_passed\": true, \"error\": null, \"implementation_notes\": \"\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-21T20:54:31.763191Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 10, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-11-21 hyp-20261121-003-r10s2 (regression, +0.68%): Two-fetch lookahead let a registered replay RAM response cover instruction-bus stalls and cut timed CoreMark cycles by 10.02%, with the EX-to-IF control path into the even/odd replay-slot valid bits limiting median Gowin Fmax to 84.986 MHz against the 88.29 MHz needed for acceptance.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
