be-phase sandbox check rolls back the scribe's commit.\nformal/last_run*.log\n\n# Orchestrator-emitted per-rep summary. Phase-2 contract output written\n# by tools/orchestrator.py:write_run_summary after every round and at\n# end of main(). Derivable from log.jsonl; not worth tracking in git.\n# Without this entry, `git status` between rounds shows it as untracked\n# (since the orchestrator never `git add`s it), and the hypothesis-phase\n\n…[199416 of 202488 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:0f9985408d3def35]…\nn\\n## Verification\\n\\n- Verilator lint passed in hardware and ALTOPS modes. All seven cocotb suites passed, covering 88 cases.\\n- `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench` matched the ISS on selftest and all three random programs with ready buses and with both stall generators enabled. Stalled CoreMark reported `Correct operation validated.` and matched all five canonical CRCs (`e9f5`, `e714`, `1fd7`, `8e3a`, `fcaf`).\\n- `bash formal/run_all.sh` passed all 53 single-channel ALTOPS checks on the retimed RTL, with zero failures or retries. This includes forward-PC consistency, register consistency, and liveness.\\n\", \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-21T16:47:09.004133Z\", \"slot\": 2, \"round_id\": 6, \"lesson\": \"- 2026-11-21 hyp-20261121-003-r6s2 (regression, +8.23%): Resolved-backedge replay hid imem stalls and cut timed CoreMark cycles by 7.74%, with the predicted fetch PC path through decode admission to last-word parking capping median Gowin Fmax at 66.730 MHz, below the 70.38 MHz needed to match the divider-retimed round winner.\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
