ediate bits in parallel with direction lookup and\\nfeed it directly into the existing boundary admission and parking logic.\\n\\nSplit the 18-bit in-window word sum into two nine-bit groups. Compute\\nboth local sums, the upper group's carry generate and propagate, and\\nthe lower carry in parallel. Increment the upper \n24:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261121-002-r8s1\", \"title\": \"Sp\n…[1261 of 4333 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:59a9efed50d23e03]…\nfor training. This\\nnarrows the fetch queue payload and takes training out of decode.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Make IF own the outstanding request and a fall-through FIFO of ready\\ninstruction words. Each 64-bit entry carries the raw instruction, full\\nword PC, issued taken prediction, and a last-mapped-word marker. Remove\\nthe full architectural direct target from the FIFO and ID/EX. Compute\\nthe full RV32 B/J target in EX from the registered PC and immediate\\nalongside the branch comparison. Derive direct target misalignment\\nfrom immediate bit 1 so link eligibility stays off the target adder.\\nFeed the full EX result to the existing registered correction path\\nand use it for RVFI next-P\ne431ca7 log: hyp-20261121-003-r8s2 regression\na833f17 log: hyp-20261121-002-r8s1 improvement\n1abdece log: hyp-20261121-001-r8s0 regression\ne80f9ca hyp-20261121-002-r8s1: Split speculative fetch from branch resolution and training (+6.4%)\nc3bc8fc log: hyp-20261121-003-r7s2 regression\nd16ec11 log: hyp-20261121-002-r7s1 improvement\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
