{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_133","type":"agent_message","text":"I kept the fastest measured version. Gowin reported 79.285, 75.288, and 75.288 MHz, which gives 206.35 iterations/sec at the measured cycle count. That falls short of the acceptance margin. The selected RTL passed lint, cocotb, and co-simulation. Only the formal register-consistency check remains in progress."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_134","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'check_dir=\"$TMPDIR/bench-formal.toWKNF7F/formal/riscv-formal/cores/bench-ReplayQueue/checks\"; find \"$check_dir\" -maxdepth 1 -name '\"'*.sby' | wc -l; rg -c '<testcase' cores/bench/test/test_pipeline_runner.result.xml; sed -n '1,120p' implementation_notes.md; date -u\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_134","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'check_dir=\"$TMPDIR/bench-formal.toWKNF7F/formal/riscv-formal/cores/bench-ReplayQueue/checks\"; find \"$check_dir\" -maxdepth 1 -name '\"'*.sby' | wc -l; rg -c '<testcase' cores/bench/test/test_pipeline_runner.result.xml; sed -n '1,120p' implementation_notes.md; date -u\"","aggregated_output":"53\n36\n# Parallel instruction replay\n\nFetch stages each advancing, legal, aligned, taken conditional backedge and tracks one inclusive range of up to 128 words. A contained backedge retains the active range. Accepted matching bus words in the range fill both synchronous RAMs through a staged write. Each copy carries the instruction, page bit, B/J target bits [21:1], and eligible JAL and branch predecode bits.\n\nThe RAMs read PC+4 and the direct target index every cycle. A seven-bit sum computes the bus target index. Registered direction selects the response after the edge. Fetch checks the selected index, page and word validity, and suppresses a read that coincided with a refill at that index. The producer retains a qualified response across a hold. A matching ready bus word has priority, and a stale response is discarded even if the producer has returned to the request address.\n\nThe five-entry queue retains empty fall-through. It records a bypass consumption separately so replay data does not drive the buffered head's pop control. Registered EX recovery supplies the corrected bus address and clears younger queue entries. Fetch marks the last mapped word and parks on bus admission. The marked instruction forces recovery to its resolved successor when it advances. Accepted overlapping stores and advancing FENCE.I clear replay state at the edge, and FENCE.I also refetches PC+4. A physical refill concurrent with invalidation has no valid entry after the edge.\n\nDirected tests cover selection of both successors, halfword-alignment traps from replay, two-page and nested ranges, a full queue retaining a replay response, refill collisions, ready stale responses, recovery overriding a held request, last-word admission and squash, and code updates through a store and FENCE.I.\n\n## Local verification\n\n- Verilator lint passed with no warnings. The cocotb suite passed all seven runners, including 36 pipeline cases.\n- RVFI co-simulation passed for selftest and three randomized programs in both readiness modes. The canonical stalled CoreMark run passed at 3,648,511 bracketed cycles over ten iterations, down 7.78% from the champion. The start and stop markers occurred at cycles 13,171 and 3,661,682.\n- CoreMark reported `seedcrc=0xe9f5`, `crclist=0xe714`, `crcmatrix=0x1fd7`, `crcstate=0x8e3a`, `crcfinal=0xfcaf`, and `Correct operation validated.`\n- The single-channel formal run has 52 passing checks, including liveness, unique retirement order, both PC checks, and the illegal-instruction check. `reg_ch0` is still solving with no counterexample reported.\n\nThe formal and co-simulation commands use scratch copies of the existing harnesses and benchmark inputs. The formal wrapper ties both readiness inputs high. The directed tests and stalled co-simulation exercise replay with changing readiness.\n\n## Gowin timing\n\n| Placement | Fmax (MHz) | Worst setup path |\n| --- | ---: | --- |\n| 0 | 79.285 | Direct replay block RAM to the ID/EX operand through the register file |\n| 1 | 75.288 | Registered direct recovery select to predicted fetch PC |\n| 2 | 75.288 | Registered direct recovery select to predicted fetch PC |\n\nThe median was 75.288 MHz. At 3,648,511 bracketed cycles, that yields 206.35 iterations/sec, 2.65% below the champion. The 4.6% acceptance margin requires 80.90 MHz at this cycle count. The selected implementation had the highest median of the locally measured variants. It used 5,170 logic cells, 2,006 registers, nine block RAMs and nine DSPs.\nSat Nov 21 18:05:21 UTC 2026\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
