ame-cycle forwarding into the divider seed nearly tied for the Gowin timing limit, so the 72.222 MHz median lost to the round winner, which registered divider inputs and reached 76.281 MHz at the same CoreMark cycle count.\n19:- 2026-11-21 hyp-20261121-001-r7s0 (regression, +4.69%): Checking the B/J window from the original PC page and adder carry and hashing PC candidates before the fetch mux moved Gowin's setup limit from JALR recovery to low-word MUL, so at unchanged CoreMark cycles the final 79.858 MHz median (83.632 MHz in scratch) yielded a smaller gain than the round's reciprocal-divider pipeline.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
