{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_8", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"ls -ld /srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_2-sol_xhigh-v2-rep4/formal/riscv-formal; cat .gitignore; cat cores/bench/LESSONS.md | tail -100; rg -n 'champion|388|3,58|252\\\\.90|late branch' cores/bench/experiments -g '\"'!*.v'\"'\"", "aggregated_output": "drwxrwx---+ 14 nobody nogroup 4096 Nov 21 15:16 /srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_2-sol_xhigh-v2-rep4/formal/riscv-formal\n# Python\n__pycache__/\n*.pyc\n*.pyo\n.pytest_cache/\n.mypy_cache/\n\n# Toolchain (downloaded by setup.sh)\n.toolchain/\n\n# Vendored as submodule (initialized in Phase 4). No trailing slash so the\n# pattern matches both the cloned directory in the main repo AND the\n# symlink that worktree.py creates inside each worktree (otherwise git\n# status flags the symlink as untracked and sandbox check trips).\nformal/riscv-formal\n\n# Formal run output (regenerated per run; surfaced via stdout to the orchestrator).\n# Glob covers both the legacy single-file path and the PID-suffixed variants\n# emitted by run_all.sh after the concurrent-rm-race fix (formal/run_all.sh\n# writes last_run-<pid>.log so simultaneous invocations don't truncate each\n# other). Without the glob, `git status` lists the per-PID logs as untracked\n# and the scribe-phase sandbox check rolls back the scribe's commit.\nformal/last_run*.log\n\n# Orchestrator-emitted per-rep summary. Phase-2 contract output written\n# by tools/orchestrator.py:write_run_summary after every round and at\n# end of main(). Derivable from log.jsonl; not worth tracking in git.\n# Without this entry, `git status` between rounds shows it as untracked\n# (since the orchestrator never `git add`s it), and the hypothesis-phase\n# sandbox check in tools/agents/hypothesis.py rolls back the next slot's\n# turn with \"modified off-limits paths: ['.../run_summary.json']\".\n# Caught live during the gpt-5.5 effort sweep — slot 2 in round 2 of\n# every rep was hypothesis_gen_fai