{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_165","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"git diff --check && git status --short && sed -n '1,135p' cores/bench/implementation_notes.md\"","aggregated_output":" M cores/bench/rtl/core.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/core_pkg.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/ex_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/if_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/rtl/mem_stage.sv\n M cores/bench/test/test_pipeline.py\n# Two-step successor hints for fetch replay\n\nFetch stages each accepted producer PC for training. A three-word observation writes the oldest PC's seven-bit word index. The packed 128-entry distributed RAM stores the third PC and sets validity when that PC differs from the oldest PC plus eight. Registered EX recovery starts a new history. Reset and advancing FENCE.I discard pending training and sweep the table alongside the replay RAM.\n\nA hint steers the existing synchronous RAM read. The full replay RAM tag and the slot's producer PC qualify the payload. Collision checking uses the read response's captured write enable and indices. The fill uses the successor and boundary flag already captured in the producer register on the bus-accept edge. A ready response on the registered recovery cycle predicts PC+4. Ordinary B/J prediction starts at the producer register.\n\nFor timing, the design registers the branch direction index with the next producer PC and computes the upper and lower B/J target sums in parallel. EX produces the individual recovery selects alongside the immediate squash and registers the data-access alignment check before MEM. The alignment check still gates the same bus operations and retirement fields.\n\nThe directed tests check a taken path replayed during a held bus request, sequential observations clearing the hint, source and replay tag aliases, rejection of a colliding RAM response, ordered RVFI, and FENCE.I clearing a warm table. Untagged source aliases can reduce replay hit rate. The last mapped word is excluded from hint history and replay, so it still requires bus acceptance.\n\n## Local verification\n\n- Verilator lint passed without warnings. All 36 pipeline tests passed. RVFI co-simulation passed for selftest and all three random traces with and without stalls.\n- CoreMark completed 10 iterations in 3,471,586 bracketed cycles with all five canonical CRCs and the validated-operation message. This is 2.43% fewer cycles than the champion.\n- Gowin options 0, 1, and 2 measured 83.341, 89.954, and 89.954 MHz. The 89.954 MHz median gives 259.11 iterations/s, 2.46% above the champion and below the 92.3 MHz target. The median placements were limited by EX operand forwarding through branch resolution into predictor training.\n- The first RTL version passed all 53 local formal checks. The final timing build is running through the same gate.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
