th a 199.837 ns, 156-cell path through\\\\noperand forwarding and the EX ALU. The signed and unsigned division and\\\\nremainder operators are the likely source of that depth. Their outputs feed\\\\nthe same registered result used for forwarding and data addresses, so their\\\\ntiming limits the clock for every instruction. A baseline retirement trace\\\\nwith both bus stalls enabled reproduced the 4,491,485 timed cycles and all\\\\nfive reference CRCs. It contained two divide or remainder instructions in\\\\nthe full run and zero between the timing markers.\\\\n\\\", \\\"hypothesis\\\": {\\\"motivation\\\": \\\"The bench \n…[90654 of 93726 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:2fa5952191f3f3ad]…\ns with all five canonical CRCs and `Correct operation validated.`\\\\n- `make fpga TARGET=bench` measured 54.459, 54.759, and 54.759 MHz across the placements, with a 54.759 MHz median and a fitness of 121.92 iterations/s. Placement 0 used 2,751 logic cells, 660 registers, and two DSPs.\\\\n\\\\nThe area increased from the champion's 2,664 logic cells and 565 registers. The low-word multiply path is the worst setup path in all three placements, with divider feedback nearly tied in placements 1 and 2.\\\\n\\\", \\\"timestamp\\\": \\\"2026-11-21T14:03:08.189491Z\\\", \\\"slot\\\": 0, \\\"round_id\\\": 2, \\\"lesson\\\": \\\"- 2026-11-21 hyp-20261121-001-r2s0 (improvement, +13.61%): Registered high-product correction, a parallelized four-bit divider seed, and wrong-path squashes via ID/EX validity shortened EX arithmetic and redirect-to-load-use feedback paths, raising median Gowin Fmax from 48.196 to 54.759 MHz while keeping CoreMark\\\\u2019s hot MUL single-cycle and preserving its timed cycle count.\\\"}\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
