{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20261121-001-r3s0.last cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/.agent.hyp-20261121-003-r3s2.last'","aggregated_output":"Wrote and schema-validated [hyp-20261121-001-r3s0.yaml](/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_2-sol_xhigh-v2-rep4/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261121-001-r3s0-hypgen/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261121-001-r3s0.yaml). It proposes a dedicated EX memory-address path and parallel radix-4 divider feedback while keeping `MUL` single-cycle.\n\nA scratch prototype reached **135.52 CoreMark iter/s (+11.15%)** at 60.868 MHz median Gowin Fmax and 4,491,485 timed cycles. It passed all 53 ALTOPS formal checks, cocotb, and stalled cosimulation with the canonical CoreMark CRCs.Wrote and schema-validated the `cores/bench` predictor hypothesis. It uses a 64-entry direction table and computes direct targets from the fetched instruction. A bounds check keeps speculative conditional fetches within instruction memory. [hyp-20261121-003-r3s2.yaml](/srv/hwebench/clones/gpt-6_2-sol_xhigh-v2-rep4/cores/bench/worktrees/hyp-20261121-003-r3s2-hypgen/cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261121-003-r3s2.yaml)\n\nThe guarded scratch prototype scored **137.42 CoreMark iter/sec**, **12.72% above** the 121.92 champion, with 4,190,307 bracketed cycles and a 57.585 MHz Gowin median. Canonical CRC validation, all 53 single-issue formal checks, and all seven cocotb runners passed.","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
