nst the 51.15 MHz needed to match the EX-tuned champion.\n- 2026-11-21 hyp-20261121-003-r2s2 (regression, +8.73%): The forwarded ALU path limited the tagged BTB with parallel EX successor checks to 48.845 MHz median Gowin Fmax, below the 51.04 MHz needed to match the round’s EX-tuned winner after a 6.79% cut in stalled CoreMark cycles.\n- 2026-11-21 hyp-20261121-001-r3s0 (regression, +9.83%): A dedicated EX/MEM effective address took the ALU/MUL result mux off the data RAM address path and two radix-4 steps per cycle shortened divider feedback, yielding a clock-driven CoreMark gain that the round’s direction-only fetch predictor surpassed by avoiding taken-transfer bubbles.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
