th younger instructions\n  and register the selected recovery request before it drives fetch. Carry\n  its window, boundary and PC+4 metadata alongside the address. Predict the\n  first corrected word sequentially to keep the new recovery select off the\n  ordinary predictor and target arithmetic. Preserve stal\n…[1733 of 4805 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:0097ef078bdd34ef]…\n EX work on a late correction.\"\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \"Expose the formatted load value and qualified write status for operand reporting and fallback. Carry the late branch's successor and trap and hold its single-channel retirement during a correction.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Adopt the registered late correction and its precomputed sequential successor. Keep the comparison off fetch queue feedback and preserve immediate uncontested EX training and ordered updates on collisions.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Wire the raw load response, producer status and late correction between stages while preserving the single-retirement interface.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Cover every byte lane, both halfword lanes, matching both branch sources, misaligned producer fallback, small-offset address carries and wraparound, and stalls. Check exact RVFI operands and order, suppressed wrong-path stores, and liveness with a corrected-path divide.\"\n.\n..\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
