{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_59", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat > cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261121-001-r10s0.yaml <<'YAML'\nid: hyp-20261121-001-r10s0\ntitle: \\\"Bypass load data directly into equality branch resolution\\\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The bench champion scores 237.13 CoreMark iterations per second at\n  93.810 MHz in 3,956,104 timed cycles. A scratch CoreMark profile counted\n  about 132,000 load-use bubbles before BEQ or BNE, two-thirds of all\n  load-use bubbles. A scratch equality-branch bypass passed canonical CRC\n  validation in 3,844,873 timed cycles. Its direct path from the data RAM\n  through load formatting and branch training cut placement-1 Fmax to\n  72.147 MHz, so the useful cycle reduction needs a shorter bypass path.\nhypothesis: |\n  Allow a legal BEQ or BNE to issue directly behind an aligned load it\n  depends on. Keep the bypass local to the branch equality comparator.\n  Compare the raw memory word with the other forwarded operand in parallel\n  by access width. For a byte or halfword, check the other operand's upper\n  bits against the required sign or zero extension of its own low bits.\n  In parallel, compare those low bits with the raw memory lanes, then use\n  the registered load width and address to select the comparison. A word\n  load compares all 32 bits directly. If both sources select the same load,\n  equality is true. Preserve the formatted load path for writeback and\n  RVFI. Keep the existing interlock for every other load-use pair.\n\n  Precompute the sequential and direct correction enables for each\n  possible equality outcome from the registered branch type, prediction,\n  alignment and boundary flags. Select the enables with the load\n  comparison and capture them in the existing IF recovery registers when\n  the load is accepted. Use the registered correction to suppress all\n  effects of the speculatively captured younger EX instruction while ID\n  accepts the corrected fetch. Gate off younger bypass eligibility and\n  MUL/DIV launch on that edge. Keep ordinary EX recovery on its existing\n  schedule. Capture the equality outcome for the late branch's ordered RVFI\n  retirement and report the actual loaded source values.\n\n  Keep predictor RAM lookup and saturating counter arithmetic off the\n  load-response path. Register the incremented and decremented counter\n  candidates in parallel with the branch outcome, then select the pending\n  update with the registered outcome and forward that same value on an\n  index alias. Qualify training with the registered alignment so a trapped\n  taken branch cannot update the table. Keep the predictor policy, memory\n  handshake and single-channel retirement contract. At approximately\n  3.845 million cycles, the required median Gowin Fmax is above 95.4 MHz.\n  A median of 96.7 MHz would yield about 6% higher fitness. The raw-lane\n  comparison and prequalified recovery and training paths are the timing\n  hypothesis and need measurement together.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 6\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/hazard_unit.sv\n    description: \\\"Exempt the qualified load-to-BEQ/BNE pair from the load-use bubble and retain all other interlocks and data backpressure.\\\"\n  - file: rtl/core_pkg.sv\n    description: \\\"Carry the load-branch bypass metadata and qualified outcome with the existing pipeline registers.\\\"\n  - file: rtl/id_stage.sv\n    description: \\\"Latch the qualified equality-branch dependency and operands with the ordinary issue and flush controls.\\\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \\\"Use the raw-lane equality bypass for qualified pairs, form correction enables in parallel, and cancel all younger EX effects on a registered late correction.\\\"\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: \\\"Expose the current load lane metadata and preserve formatted load forwarding, alignment checks and the resolved branch's RVFI payload.\\\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \\\"Capture the prequalified correction enables and select a precomputed training counter using the registered outcome, retaining recovery priority, parking and alias forwarding.\\\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \\\"Wire the equality bypass, registered squash and training controls without changing either memory interface or the NRET=1 RVFI ports.\\\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \\\"Check signed and unsigned subword comparisons, two matching sources, misaligned loads, a stalled load, and a recovery that squashes a younger store or divide. Retain the existing legality, raw-source and retirement checks.\\\"\nYAML\npython - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport jsonschema\nimport yaml\nfile = Path('cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261121-001-r10s0.yaml')\nproposal = yaml.safe_load(file.read_text())\njsonschema.validate(proposal, json.loads(Path('schemas/hypothesis.schema.json').read_text()))\nassert proposal['id'] == file.stem\nassert proposal['category'] == 'micro_opt'\nassert type(proposal['expected_impact']['fitness_delta_pct']) is int\nassert all((Path('cores/bench') / change['file']).is_file() for change in proposal['changes'])\nprint('Validated schema, ID, category and all eight bench-relative change paths.')\nprint('Projected break-even for acceptance at measured cycles:', 93.810 * 1.046 * 3844873 / 3956104)\nPY\ngit status --short --untracked-files=all\"", "aggregated_output": "", "exit_code": null, "status": "in_progress"}}
