{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_92","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261121-001-r11s0.yaml'","aggregated_output":"id: hyp-20261121-001-r11s0\ntitle: Share one registered PC for direct and fall-through recovery\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The bench champion scores 237.13 CoreMark iterations per second at\n  93.810 MHz and 3,956,104 timed cycles. The two median Gowin placements\n  are limited by forwarding through the branch comparator into IF recovery\n  selection. The direct and fall-through recovery registers and their\n  address and flag muxes also compete for routing in IF. A failed direct\n  prediction must use the successor opposite to the prediction carried\n  into EX. That candidate PC can be formed while the comparison runs.\nhypothesis: |\n  In EX select a signed word displacement from the registered prediction\n  bit. Use +1 if IF predicted taken and the decoded B/J word displacement\n  if IF predicted sequential. Add it to the 30-bit word PC with normal\n  modulo-2^32 byte-address wrap. IF captures the candidate and its window\n  flags in one recovery bank. An advancing non-JALR instruction selects\n  this bank only when its actual legal, aligned direct transfer outcome\n  disagrees with its prediction. The comparator feeds the request enable\n  while the PC calculation depends on the registered prediction and\n  displacement. Preserve the exact resolved successor for RVFI and the\n  link value for JAL and JALR.\n\n  IF suppresses taken predictions at the last mapped word. A taken\n  aligned direct transfer there therefore uses the candidate bank.\n  Fall-through and traps at that word select the constant 0x00100000\n  through a dedicated recovery flag. An advancing legal, aligned JALR\n  independently selects its registered EX/MEM effective address with\n  bit zero cleared. Qualify all recovery requests with EX advance and\n  combine them for the existing same-edge ID squash. Keep the corrected\n  fetch on the next cycle and preserve request holding, queue parking,\n  predictor training, alignment traps, and single-channel retirement.\n\n  At 3,956,104 timed cycles the acceptance threshold is above 98.13 MHz\n  median Gowin Fmax. A 100 MHz median would yield about 253 iterations\n  per second. Check timing of the merged candidate adder as well as\n  the comparator-to-redirect and indirect-target feedback paths. Recheck\n  the full single-channel formal gate and stalled CoreMark CRCs.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 7\n  confidence: low\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: Form the opposite successor from the prediction bit and emit separate candidate, boundary fall-through, and aligned indirect recovery requests.\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: Replace the two wide direct and sequential context registers with one candidate bank and a constant mapped-edge successor. Select the corresponding flags with the request address.\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: Route the candidate and mutually exclusive recovery requests and preserve the common decode squash and external interfaces.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: Check both branch misprediction directions, aligned direct and trapped transfers at the mapped edge, and stalls during corrected fetches with ordered retirement.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
