{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_5", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n '\\\"category\\\": \\\"micro_opt\\\"' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | cut -d: -f2- | python3 -c 'import sys,json; [(lambda e: print(json.dumps({k:e.get(k) for k in (\\\"id\\\",\\\"title\\\",\\\"cycles\\\",\\\"fmax_mhz\\\",\\\"critical_path\\\",\\\"implementation_notes\\\")})))(json.loads(line)) for line in sys.stdin]'\"", "aggregated_output": "{\"id\": \"baseline-bench-29c86c4\", \"title\": \"Baseline retest for cores/bench\", \"cycles\": 4491485, \"fmax_mhz\": 5.442, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_mem/reg_q.rd_3_s0\", \"to\": \"dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -189.542, \"arrival_ns\": 199.837, \"logic_cells\": 156, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_fwd\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"implementation_notes\": \"\"}\n{\"id\": \"hyp-20261121-001-r1s0\", \"title\": \"Replace the combinational divider with a shared iterative unit\", \"cycles\": 4491485, \"fmax_mhz\": 48.196, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s\", \"to\": \"dmem_1_dmem_1_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -16.035, \"arrival_ns\": 26.329, \"logic_cells\": 14, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"implementation_notes\": \"# Shared iterative divider for `cores/bench`\\n\\n`DIV`, `DIVU`, `REM`, and `REMU` share one EX divider. It captures the forwarded operands on issue and processes a 35-bit padded dividend in seven cycles of five restoring steps. EX transfers the sign-corrected result through the existing EX/MEM register, adding eight cycles to each divide or remainder instruction.\\n\\nEX waits for an older data access to advance before launching. While the divider runs, the fetch PC and ID/EX register hold and EX/MEM receives bubbles with their side-effect controls cleared. EX retains the issued operands for RVFI after the forwarding sources drain. Completion is consumed on the EX/MEM transfer edge. The `RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS` arithmetic substitutes use the same schedule.\\n\\nThe restoring steps naturally produce an all-ones quotient and the original dividend magnitude for a zero divisor. Issue logic suppresses quotient negation for that case and still sign-corrects the remainder. Signed `INT_MIN / -1` produces `0x80000000` and a zero remainder through the normal datapath. Divider tests live in `test_div_unit.py` so the existing cocotb runner can exercise the clocked divider and combinational ALU as separate tops. A guarded include in `core.sv` makes the pipeline types available for the requested glob-order lint command.\\n\\n## Local verification\\n\\n- Verilator strict lint passed with hardware arithmetic and with ALTOPS.\\n- Cocotb passed 72 tests across six suites. The divider suite covers the original arithmetic vectors, additional operand ranges, consecutive launches, backpressure, and reset. The pipeline test holds a store for three cycles and checks one accepted write, one retirement per instruction, forwarded operand reporting, and immediate use of the quotient.\\n- `formal/run_all.sh` passed all 53 single-channel checks, including liveness and all four divider instructions. The gate used ALTOPS and ready buses. Cocotb and co-simulation exercised the hardware arithmetic and memory stalls.\\n- Co-simulation passed for selftest and the three random programs with ready buses and with both stall generators enabled. CoreMark validated all five reference CRCs, retired EBREAK, and reported no out-of-bounds access.\\n\\n## Gowin and CoreMark\\n\\n| Measurement | Baseline retest | Iterative divider |\\n| --- | ---: | ---: |\\n| Median Gowin Fmax | 5.442 MHz | 48.196 MHz |\\n| CoreMark cycles between markers | 4,491,485 | 4,491,485 |\\n| CoreMark iterations per second | 12.12 | 107.31 |\\n\\nGowin placement options 0, 1, and 2 reached 47.541, 48.196, and 48.196 MHz. Option 0 used 2,664 logic cells and 565 registers. Its worst reported path crossed the register-file and ALU datapath at 26.329 ns. The divider feedback path reached 26.309 ns in the same placement.\\n\"}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
