Gowin Fmax at 48.391 MHz against the 51.15 MHz needed to match the EX-tuned champion.\n- 2026-11-21 hyp-20261121-003-r2s2 (regression, +8.73%): The forwarded ALU path limited the tagged BTB with parallel EX successor checks to 48.845 MHz median Gowin Fmax, below the 51.04 MHz needed to match t\n…[1431 of 4503 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:0b01e7dff92ff3a1]…\nnLength\": 5},\n    \"category\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"micro_opt\",\"structural\",\"extension\",\"predictor\",\"memory\"]},\n    \"motivation\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"hypothesis\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"expected_impact\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"required\": [\"fitness_delta_pct\",\"confidence\"],\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"fitness_delta_pct\": {\"type\": \"integer\"},\n        \"confidence\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"low\",\"medium\",\"high\"]}\n      }\n    },\n    \"changes\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\", \"minItems\": 1,\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"required\": [\"file\",\"description\"],\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"file\":        {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"Must be under rtl/ (any extension) or be a test/test_*.py cocotb suite. Anything else is rejected by the runtime sandbox check.\",\n            \"pattern\": \"^(rtl/[^.].*|test/test_[^/]+\\\\.py)$\"\n          },\n          \"description\": {\"type\": \"string\"}\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"rg '\\\"category\\\": \\\"micro_opt\\\"' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | jq -r 'select(.id | startswith(\\\"hyp\\\")) | [.id,.title,.fitness,.cycles,.fmax_mhz,(.critical_path | [.from,.to,.arrival_ns,.logic_cells] | tostring),.hypothesis.hypothesis,.implementation_notes] | @tsv'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_4", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg '\\\"category\\\": \\\"micro_opt\\\"' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | jq -r 'select(.id | startswith(\\\"hyp\\\")) | [.id,.title,.fitness,.cycles,.fmax_mhz,(.critical_path | [.from,.to,.arrival_ns,.logic_cells] | tostring),.hypothesis.hypothesis,.implementation_notes] | @tsv'\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261121-001-r1s0\tReplace the combinational divider with a shared iterative unit\t107.31\t4491485\t48.196\t[\"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s\",\"dmem_1_dmem_1_0_0_s\",26.329,14]\tReplace all four combinational division and remainder operations with one EX\\ndivider that computes a quotient and remainder with unsigned restoring steps.\\nRegister the operand magnitudes and sign bits on issue. Pad the dividend\\nmagnitude to 35 bits and perform five restoring steps per cycle for seven\\ncycles. Select and sign-correct the registered result on EX/MEM transfer.\\nThe feedback path then contains at most five subtract-and-select steps. This\\nschedule adds eight EX cycles and fits the existing 10-cycle liveness window\\nwith ready buses, including a preceding redirect or load-use bubble. Keep the\\nsame schedule under RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS using the existing arithmetic\\nsubstitutes so formal exercises issue, backpressure and completion. Other\\noperations retain single-cycle EX. At the baseline timed cycle count, a\\nmedian Gowin Fmax of 8.16 MHz yields about 50% higher fitness. Evaluate both\\nthe marker-bracketed cycle count and Fmax because the added setup cycles can\\nshift the pseudo-random stall sequence.\\n\t# Shared iterative divider for `cores/bench`\\n\\n`DIV`, `DIVU`, `REM`, and `REMU` share one EX divider. It captures the forwarded operands on issue and processes a 35-bit padded dividend in seven cycles of five restoring steps. EX transfers the sign-corrected result through the existing EX/MEM register, adding eight cycles to each divide or remainder instruction.\\n\\nEX waits for an older data access to advance before launching. While the divider runs, the fetch PC and ID/EX register hold and EX/MEM receives bubbles with their side-effect controls cleared. EX retains the issued operands for RVFI after the forwarding sources drain. Completion is consumed on the EX/MEM transfer edge. The `RISCV_FORMAL_ALTOPS` arithmetic substitutes use the same schedule.\\n\\nThe restoring steps naturally produce an all-ones quotient and the original dividen\n…[7758 of 10830 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:22b9ec6223803eee]…\nering three times the unsigned divisor magnitude in parallel.\\nA divisor of at least 256 cannot take any of those four quotient bits.\\nFor the remaining six iterations use two radix-4 steps per cycle. Each\\nstep tries the widened subtractions of D, 2D and 3D in parallel and\\nselects the remainder from the largest multiple that fits. Use a 34-bit\\nshifted remainder and divisor multiples with a 35-bit subtraction to keep\\nthe borrow. This cuts the wide subtract-and-select chain from four to two.\\n\\nThe scratch implementation measured 63.182, 60.868 and 60.868 MHz across\\nGowin placements. Stalled CoreMark validated all five canonical CRCs in\\n4,491,485 timed cycles, giving 135.52 iter/s, up 11.15%. Placement 0 used\\n3,022 logic cells and 726 registers. The prototype passed 53 single-channel\\nALTOPS checks, all seven cocotb runners, and selftest plus three random\\nRVFI traces with ready and stalled buses. Directed checks passed for the\\n255/256 divisor boundary and a stalled byte store with a forwarded base.\\n\t\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
