unter snapshot under the existing\nID/EX register enable, qualify them with the instruction's validity, and\nhold them through backpressure. Update the counter once per advancing\nnontrapping conditional branch. Forward same-index writes to the admitted\ninstruction's counter snapshot for training. The pre-edge counter controls\nthe fetch successor.\n\nOn an advancing valid EX instruction, compare the recor\n…[4805 of 7877 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:613cf4ad1bb3b232]…\nng`\n161:                \"fmax_mhz\": None, \"timed_out\": True,\n185:                \"seeds\": [r.get(\"fmax_mhz\") for r in results],\n190:        \"fmax_mhz\": round(statistics.median(r[\"fmax_mhz\"] for r in results), 3),\n191:        \"seeds\": [r[\"fmax_mhz\"] for r in results],\n192:        \"perturbations\": [[r[\"place_option\"], r[\"fmax_mhz\"], r[\"levels\"]] for r in results],\n195:        \"critical_path\": (ref.get(\"critical_paths\") or [None])[0],\n200:    \"\"\"`make timing TARGET=<core>`: the vendor timing the evaluator scores,\n214:                                wt / \"cores\" / a.target / \"generated\" / \"timing\", options=opts)\n219:        print(f\"place_option {r['place_option']}: Fmax {r['fmax_mhz']} MHz, {r['levels']} logic levels; \"\n221:        tr = (wt / \"cores\" / a.target / \"generated\" / \"timing\" / f\"gowin_p{r['place_option']}\" / \"impl/pnr/core_bench.tr\")\n222:        for i, p in enumerate(critical_paths(tr.read_text(errors=\"replace\"), a.paths), 1):\n227:        print(f\"score Fmax (median): {summarize(res)['fmax_mhz']} MHz\")\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
