{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"rg '\\\"category\\\"\\\\s*:\\\\s*\\\"micro_opt\\\"' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python3 -c 'import sys,json; ks=(\\\"id\\\",\\\"title\\\",\\\"cycles\\\",\\\"fmax_mhz\\\",\\\"critical_path\\\"); [print(json.dumps({k:d.get(k) for k in ks}), (d.get(\\\"implementation_notes\\\", \\\"\\\").split(\\\"## Local verification\\\")[0] if \\\"r4s0\\\" in d[\\\"id\\\"] else \\\"\\\")) for d in map(json.loads,sys.stdin)]'\"","aggregated_output":"{\"id\": \"baseline-bench-29c86c4\", \"title\": \"Baseline retest for cores/bench\", \"cycles\": 4491485, \"fmax_mhz\": 5.442, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_mem/reg_q.rd_3_s0\", \"to\": \"dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -189.542, \"arrival_ns\": 199.837, \"logic_cells\": 156, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_fwd\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}} \n{\"id\": \"hyp-20261121-001-r1s0\", \"title\": \"Replace the combinational divider with a shared iterative unit\", \"cycles\": 4491485, \"fmax_mhz\": 48.196, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s\", \"to\": \"dmem_1_dmem_1_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -16.035, \"arrival_ns\": 26.329, \"logic_cells\": 14, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}} \n{\"id\": \"hyp-20261121-001-r2s0\", \"title\": \"Shorten execute timing paths at the current pipeline depth\", \"cycles\": 4491485, \"fmax_mhz\": 54.759, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s\", \"to\": \"dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -13.362, \"arrival_ns\": 23.657, \"logic_cells\": 12, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_mul\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}} \n{\"id\": \"hyp-20261121-001-r3s0\", \"title\": \"Split the EX address path and shorten divider feedback\", \"cycles\": 4491485, \"fmax_mhz\": 60.145, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_rf/regs_regs_0_0_s\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/u_div/remainder_q_3_s1\", \"slack_ns\": -11.905, \"arrival_ns\": 22.199, \"logic_cells\": 16, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_id\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_div\"]}} \n{\"id\": \"hyp-20261121-001-r4s0\", \"title\": \"Split and parallelize the EX operand-to-result path\", \"cycles\": 4190307, \"fmax_mhz\": 64.657, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_mem/reg_q.rd_0_s0\", \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/reg_q.alu_result_21_s0\", \"slack_ns\": -10.978, \"arrival_ns\": 21.272, \"logic_cells\": 34, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_fwd\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}} # Bench EX datapath implementation\n\n- EX computes the effective address from forwarded `rs1` and the decoded I- or S-type immediate. The 12-bit sum runs in parallel with three upper-word candidates. EX/MEM holds the full address with the store payload and memory controls through data-bus stalls. MEM uses it for the bus address, alignment, lane masks, load extraction, and aligned RVFI address.\n- EX ORs five independently masked results for the jump link, low multiply, high multiply, division or remainder, and base ALU. This preserves the forwarding schedule, branch prediction, load-use interlock, and single-cycle low `MUL`.\n- The two asynchronous register reads share one 32-word distributed RAM array. Reset clears the written bits. Reads retain hardwired `x0` and matching-write priority on both ports.\n- The divider launches with four seed bits, consumes four more bits with eight-bit restoring arithmetic while registering `3D`, then performs two radix-4 steps on each of six edges. Each radix-4 step compares all three multiples in parallel. The hardware and ALTOPS paths retain the launch-to-completion schedule and hold completion until consumed.\n\nJALR also uses the split address adder because it has the same signed 12-bit offset. It still clears target bit zero before redirecting. The existing four-bit divider seed computes the magnitude of its two high bit pairs with independent carry inputs to shorten the launch path.\n\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
