{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_9", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n 'hyp-20261121-00[123]-r5s[012]' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python3 -c 'import json,sys; keys=(\\\"hypothesis\\\", \\\"implementation_notes\\\"); [print(x[\\\"id\\\"],*(str(x.get(k)) for k in keys),sep=\\\"\\\\n\\\") for line in sys.stdin for n,s in [line.split(\\\":\\\",1)] for x in [json.loads(s)]]'\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261121-001-r5s0\n{'motivation': 'The 154.30 iter/sec champion runs at 64.657 MHz with 4,190,307 timed\\nCoreMark cycles. Its reported 21.272 ns setup path starts at a MEM/WB\\ndestination bit and crosses the forwarding comparisons and operand muxes\\ninto the integer ALU and EX/MEM result register. The other two Gowin\\nplacements were limited by forwarding into the divide launch seed. EX\\ncan start with register matches that ID already computed.\\n', 'hypothesis': \"Retiming bypass selection across the existing ID/EX boundary should\\nshorten the forwarded-operand paths to the ALU, effective-address adder,\\nbranch resolution and M-unit launch. At ID admission compare each raw\\nsource field against the current EX and MEM destinations. Register both\\nnonzero match bits per source with the decoded instruction. On that edge\\nthose producers enter EX/MEM and MEM/WB respectively. In EX qualify the\\nregistered matches with each producer's staged post-trap reg_write bit.\\nUse the EX/MEM hit for its mask, the MEM/WB hit gated by the absence of\\nan EX/MEM hit for its mask, and the absence of both hits for the captured\\nRF value. When a younger matching producer traps, the older matching\\nwriter can still supply the operand. Register the selected architectural\\nwrite value at MEM/WB so the older bypass feeds EX directly from a flop.\\n\\nKeep the existing load-use interlock on both raw source fields, with the\\nsame issue, redirect and retirement schedule. During a data wait, hold\\nthe ID/EX matches, EX/MEM producer and MEM/WB forwarding payload even\\nafter clearing MEM/WB retirement valid. On the launch edge of a high\\nmultiply or divide, capture the resolved operands before older producers\\ndrain. The held instruction uses its captured operands for RVFI and its\\nM-unit result on completion. Recompute the tags for the next admitted\\ninstruction. Keep the existing M-unit timing and ALTOPS behavior.\\n\\nA scratch prototype met 75.171, 72.846 and 72.846 MHz across the three\\nGowin placements with 3,398 reported logic cells in plac\n…[15475 of 18547 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:3e6d5c43690595a1]…\n EX advancement, recovery type and PC candidates to IF, including EX/MEM effective address with bit zero cleared for JALR. Drive the existing ID/EX validity squash from the live EX mismatch.'}, {'file': 'rtl/ex_stage.sv', 'description': 'Export EX advance, the actual direct and indirect transfer selects, PC+4, and the latched direct target. Keep the actual-next-PC mux local to RVFI, preserve the one-bit mismatch check and train only on valid nontrapping branch advancement.'}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Hold an older store long enough to fill five slots, check that the full producer can resume on the cycle after a pop, and check buffered issue while imem is unready. Update the loop-exit request trace to show runahead, recovery over an unready wrong-path fetch, and a held first corrected request. Exercise JALR behind a stalled store and JALR at the last mapped word. Check links, retirement order, and wrong-path side-effect sentinels and retain the same-index training and trap cases.'}]}\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
