{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_78", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"sed -n '1,132p' cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261121-001-r6s0.yaml\"", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261121-001-r6s0\ntitle: \"Retime operand selection ahead of the EX datapath\"\ncategory: micro_opt\nmotivation: |\n  The bench champion scores 168.92 CoreMark iterations/s at 66.827 MHz\n  and 3,956,104 timed cycles. Its worst reported path starts at an ID/EX\n  source-address bit and crosses the forwarding comparisons and operand\n  mux on the way to the divider seed. The round 5 bypass experiment\n  reached 70.367 MHz on the earlier core. Applying that timing cut to the\n  current fetch queue and folding PC and immediate selection into the\n  ALU bypass mux can retain the champion's cycle count at a higher clock.\nhypothesis: |\n  Compare each raw decode source address with the current ID/EX and\n  EX/MEM destinations and register both nonzero match bits per operand\n  with ID/EX. On that admission edge the two producers advance to EX/MEM\n  and MEM/WB. In EX, qualify each match with the corresponding staged\n  register-write control. Use mutually exclusive masks for the youngest\n  eligible result, the older eligible result, and the captured register\n  read. This lets the older value win when a matching younger link traps.\n  Register the selected architectural result at MEM/WB after load\n  extension so the older bypass and WB write data come from the same\n  register. Keep the register file's same-cycle write-first bypass.\n\n  Use the three-way masked selection for the raw EX operands consumed by\n  branches, addresses, stores, M units and RVFI. In parallel, form each\n  integer ALU operand with one masked mux. Mask off all three raw choices\n  when AUIPC selects the registered PC or an immediate instruction selects\n  the registered immediate, and add that PC or immediate as the fourth\n  input. This removes the cascaded selector after the raw forwarding mux.\n\n  Keep load-use interlocking on both raw source fields and keep the match\n  bits on the ID/EX hold and squash schedule. During dmem backpressure\n  retain both bypass payloads and their write eligibility while clearing\n  MEM/WB retirement valid. Use the existing EX laun\n…[2275 of 5347 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:4af45f15c9108f9e]…\nands\n      independently with four masked inputs including PC or immediate as\n      appropriate. Keep launch-time operand capture and the existing EX\n      address generation, branch resolution and M-unit interfaces.\n  - file: rtl/mem_stage.sv\n    description: >-\n      Select load data after extension or the EX result before registering\n      MEM/WB. Keep the value and post-trap write eligibility across dmem\n      stalls while clearing retirement valid.\n  - file: rtl/wb_stage.sv\n    description: >-\n      Drive register-file and older bypass write data directly from the\n      registered MEM/WB value. Keep retirement valid in the register-file\n      write enable only.\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: >-\n      Check dual-writer priority, older-writer fallback after a younger\n      misaligned link, and a retained load operand behind a stalled store.\n      Exercise AUIPC and immediate ALU selection with raw field aliases\n      and check architectural writes, raw RVFI operands and retirement order.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
