{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_86", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'nl -ba cores/bench/experiments/hypotheses/hyp-20261121-001-r7s0.yaml && date -u'", "aggregated_output": "     1\tid: hyp-20261121-001-r7s0\n     2\ttitle: Parallelize fetch address range and predictor index computation\n     3\tcategory: micro_opt\n     4\tmotivation: |\n     5\t  The bench champion scores 192.82 CoreMark iter/s at 76.281 MHz median\n     6\t  and 3,956,104 timed cycles. In Gowin placement 0 the setup path from\n     7\t  the EX/MEM JALR address into the next predicted PC arrives at 18.558 ns,\n     8\t  within 6 ps of the reported divider path. Fetch currently selects the\n     9\t  request PC, hashes it for the prediction index, and qualifies predicted\n    10\t  targets by reducing the upper bits of the computed target. Computing\n    11\t  those two side signals in parallel cuts logic off the fetch address\n    12\t  recurrence while preserving the prediction and recovery schedule.\n    13\thypothesis: |\n    14\t  Split PC-relative target arithmetic at bit 20, the boundary of the\n    15\t  1 MiB instruction window. Add the low 18 word-address bits to the low\n    16\t  18 bits of the signed B or J word offset. The carry minus the offset\n    17\t  sign adjusts PC[31:20] by +1, 0 or -1. Form the full target from the\n    18\t  three page candidates and the low sum. In parallel, compare the\n    19\t  original page with 0xfff, 0 or 1 and combine those comparisons with\n    20\t  the same adjustment to tell whether the target page is zero. Keep\n    21\t  the target halfword alignment check. Use the same division into page\n    22\t  and word index for PC+4, and reuse the incremented page candidate.\n    23\t\n    24\t  In parallel with the request address mux, compute the existing\n    25\t  six-bit XOR hash for the predicted PC and each registered recovery\n    26\t  PC. Select the hash with the same mutually exclusive masks as the\n    27\t  request address and use it for the existing direction lookup and\n    28\t  pending-update check. Keep full 32-bit target arithmetic, predictor\n    29\t  policy and updates, fetch queue admission, last-word parking and EX\n    30\t  recovery priority. Preserve the current bus and retirement schedule.\n    31\t\n    32\t  The scratch build measured 80.204, 83.632 and 83.632 MHz across Gowin\n    33\t  placement options 0, 1 and 2 with 4,089 logic cells in option 0.\n    34\t  Low-word multiply became the longest reported path. Stalled CoreMark\n    35\t  passed the canonical CRC checks in 3,956,104 marker-bracketed cycles.\n    36\t  The measured median and cycle count imply 211.40 iter/s, 9.64 percent\n    37\t  above the champion. The acceptance floor at this cycle count is\n    38\t  about 79.79 MHz. The scratch RTL passed the existing cocotb suites,\n    39\t  the directed window-edge test and selftest plus three random ISS\n    40\t  traces with ready and stalled buses. A combinational SAT check\n    41\t  proved the target, range, increment and hash equations equivalent\n    42\t  for word-aligned requests and mutually exclusive PC selectors.\n    43\texpected_impact:\n    44\t  fitness_delta_pct: 10\n    45\t  confidence: high\n    46\tchanges:\n    47\t  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    48\t    description: >-\n    49\t      Split the direct and sequential PC arithmetic at the 1 MiB page\n    50\t      boundary. Compute target-window eligibility from the original page,\n    51\t      offset sign and low carry, and select the existing XOR index from\n    52\t      per-candidate hashes in parallel with the fetch address mux.\n    53\t  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    54\t    description: >-\n    55\t      Check fetch addresses and retirement for aligned B and J offsets\n    56\t      near the instruction window edges, including long JALs in both\n    57\t      directions, a trained-taken prediction on an untaken branch whose\n    58\t      target is one word past the last mapped PC, and an imem stall\n    59\t      during recovery. Retain the existing alias, alignment and\n    60\t      last-word parking assertions.\nSat Nov 21 17:06:55 UTC 2026\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
