{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_69", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nr = list(map(json.loads, open('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl')))[-1]\nprint(r['hypothesis']['hypothesis'])\nprint(r['implementation_notes'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "On the current bench champion, use an advancing, aligned, taken\nconditional backedge to select one replayable instruction range of up\nto 128 words inside the instruction window. Stage the EX training\nevent and its endpoints. Retain the active range for a fully contained\ninner backedge. Index synchronous replay RAM by the low seven word-PC\nbits and keep a page bit with each word to distinguish adjacent pages.\nCapture accepted bus words and their precomputed 18-bit direct target\nand eligibility. For an in-window source, form the bus target with a\n19-bit word sum and use the top bit and immediate alignment bit to\nexclude out-of-window and misaligned predictions. Register the refill\naddress, payload and range-qualified write enable before the RAM\nwrite edge. Cancel queued refills and clear word validity on range\nreplacement or invalidation, with clearing taking priority over a\ncoincident write.\n\nLaunch the next RAM lookup with the selected next producer PC. Match\nthe registered producer's full page address to the descriptor, match\nthe stored page bit, check per-word validity, and suppress replay on\na read/write collision using registered indices. Use the existing\nfolded-PC direction counter for both bus and replay words.\nA fresh ready response matching the producer takes priority. If\nreplay advances past an unready request, hold the external address\nthrough readiness and discard that response. Registered EX recovery\nsupersedes the held request and uses a fresh bus response on the\ncorrected cycle. Feed the prior trial's three-entry fall-through queue\nwith the PC, instruction and prediction bit.\n\nTreat 0x000ffffc as a fetch boundary. Accept its ready bus word once\nthrough the ordinary queue handshake, mark it in the queued payload,\nand set a producer hold at that edge. Keep the request at that address\nand suppress further acceptance until recovery. Exclude the boundary\nword from replay and defer its next-PC selection to EX. Detect the\nboundary on the producer side independently of the instruction and\npredictor result. \n…[4156 of 7228 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:91b55126bc2933d5]…\nnd a store followed by FENCE.I patching a warmed instruction.\n- `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench` passed Selftest RVFI comparison with\n  ready and stalled buses. Canonical stalled CoreMark finished with\n  seed CRC `e9f5`, list `e714`, matrix `1fd7`, state `8e3a`, final\n  `fcaf`, and “Correct operation validated.” No out-of-bounds access was\n  reported.\n\n## Gowin and CoreMark\n\n| Placement option | Fmax |\n| --- | ---: |\n| 0 | 70.738 MHz |\n| 1 | 75.282 MHz |\n| 2 | 75.282 MHz |\n| Median | 75.282 MHz |\n\nTen CoreMark iterations took **3,651,216** marker-bracketed cycles,\n7.71% fewer than the champion's 3,956,104 and 1,122 more than the prior\nreplay trial. The measured score is **206.18 iterations/sec**, 6.93%\nabove 192.82 and above the 4.6% acceptance margin. Placement zero used\n4,504 logic cells, 1,439 registers, 40 LUT-RAM cells, and six BSRAMs.\nThe divider recurrence is the worst path in all three placements.\nPlacement zero also has a close path from registered recovery selection\nto the replay RAM read address.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type": "item.started", "item": {"id": "item_70", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"cat > '/srv/hwebench/tmp/58928045/b697edee/bench-r8s0.b2RJMn/make_compact_variants.py' <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport shutil\nimport sys\n\nscratch = Path(__file__).resolve().parent\nrtl = Path('cores/bench/rtl')\n\nfor variant in sys.argv[1:]:\n    base, method = variant.split('++')\n    parent = scratch / base\n    work = scratch / variant\n    shutil.copytree(parent / rtl, work / rtl)\n    shutil.copy2(parent / 'cores/bench/core.yaml', work / 'cores/bench/core.yaml')\n    shutil.copytree(parent / 'fpga', work / 'fpga')\n\n    p = work / rtl / 'core_pkg.sv'\n    text = p.read_text().replace('    logic [31:0] direct_target;', '''    logic [19:0] target_low;\n    logic        target_page_inc;\n    logic        target_page_dec;''')\n    p.write_text(text)\n    p = work / rtl / 'if_stage.sv'\n    text = p.read_text()\n    text = text.replace('    logic [31:0] direct_target;', '''    logic [19:0] target_low;\n    logic        target_page_inc;\n    logic        target_page_dec;''')\n    text = text.replace('localparam int SLOT_WIDTH = 95;', 'localparam int SLOT_WIDTH = 85;')\n    text = text.replace('logic [31:0] sequential_pc, direct_target;', 'logic [31:0] sequential_pc;')\n    text = text.replace('  logic [11:0] pc_high, pc_high_inc, pc_high_dec, target_high;', '  logic [11:0] pc_high, pc_high_inc;')\n    text = text.replace('  logic        upper_inc, upper_dec, upper_same;', '  logic        upper_inc, upper_dec;')\n    text = text.replace('  assign pc_high_dec = pc_high - 12\\\\'d1;\\\\n', '')\n    first = text.index('  assign upper_same')\n    last = text.index('  assign page_zero', first)\n    text = text[:first] + text[last:]\n    text = text.replace('  assign produced.direct_target   = direct_target;', '''  assign produced.target_low      = {target_low, halfword_offset, 1'b0};\n  assign produced.target_page_inc = upper_inc;\n  assign produced.targ