{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg '\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20261121-(003-r11s2|003-r10s2|003-r5s2|003-r4s2|002-r11s1|001-r10s0|001-r3s0)\\\"' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python3 -c 'import json,sys; ks=\\\"id title category hypothesis fitness delta_pct fmax_mhz cycles perturbations critical_path implementation_notes\\\".split(); rows=[json.loads(l) for l in sys.stdin]; print(\\\"\\\\n\\\".join(\\\"\\\\n\\\".join(f\\\"{k}: {x[k]}\\\" for k in ks if k in x) for x in rows))'\"", "aggregated_output": "id: hyp-20261121-001-r3s0\ntitle: Split the EX address path and shorten divider feedback\ncategory: micro_opt\nhypothesis: {'motivation': 'The 121.92 iter/s champion reaches 54.759 MHz median Gowin Fmax. Its\\nworst setup path crosses EX operand selection and the low-word DSP\\nmultiply on its way to the dmem block RAM address in all three placements.\\nBase ALU results reach the same address path. Divider feedback was within\\n1 ps of the worst path in placements 1 and 2. The stalled CoreMark trace\\nhas 93,960 low-word multiplies and zero divides or remainders between the\\ntiming markers. Separating the address path can preserve the throughput of\\nthose multiplies, while shortening divider feedback raises the clock limit.\\n', 'hypothesis': 'Give the EX/MEM register a dedicated effective-address field fed by\\nforwarded rs1 plus the decoded immediate. Drive the LSU address,\\nalignment checks, lane masks and load extraction from that field. This\\nremoves the ALU and multiplier result mux from the memory address path\\nwhile keeping MUL single-cycle. Hold the address and store payload together\\nunder data bus backpressure.\\n\\nShorten the remaining divider feedback while preserving its eight wait\\ncycles. Keep the four-bit launch seed. On the first iteration, process\\nthe next four bits in a narrow eight-bit restoring datapath while\\nregistering three times the unsigned divisor magnitude in parallel.\\nA divisor of at least 256 cannot take any of those four quotient bits.\\nFor the remaining six iterations use two radix-4 steps per cycle. Each\\nstep tries the widened subtractions of D, 2D and 3D in parallel and\\nselects the remainder from the largest multiple that fits. Use a 34-bit\\nshifted remainder and divisor multiples with a 35-bit subtraction to keep\\nthe borrow. This cuts the wide subtract-and-select chain from four to two.\\n\\nThe scratch implementation measured 63.182, 60.868 and 60.868 MHz across\\nGowin placements. Stalled CoreMark validated all five canonical CRCs in\\n4,491,485 timed cycles, giving 135.52 iter/s, up \n…[46304 of 49376 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:001a3aceacc35db7]…\n recovery and stale bus handshakes.'}, {'file': 'rtl/ex_stage.sv', 'description': 'Export FENCE.I on architectural advance and use sequential recovery for it. Continue resolving replayed predictions and reporting the actual RVFI successor.'}, {'file': 'rtl/core.sv', 'description': 'Route the advancing FENCE.I event into fetch for replay invalidation.'}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Check persistent tagged replay through holds and redirects, lookup aliases, stale request disposal, and progress and code visibility during and after FENCE.I invalidation. Check ordered retirement and absent wrong-path side effects.'}]}\nfitness: 252.9\ndelta_pct: 6.65\nfmax_mhz: 89.983\ncycles: 3558019\nperturbations: [[0, 89.257, 10], [1, 89.983, 14], [2, 89.983, 14]]\ncritical_path: {'from': 'cpu/u_if/read_ptr_q_0_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_if/occupancy_q_2_s0', 'slack_ns': -6.204, 'arrival_ns': 16.498, 'logic_cells': 10, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_if', 'cpu/u_hazard', 'cpu/u_id', 'cpu/u_if']}\nimplementation_notes: \n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
