{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_52","type":"agent_message","text":"The fixed-head variants moved the timing limit to fetch recovery and EX forwarding, and direct replay admission saved only 0.6% of cycles. A profile found about 120,000 load-use bubbles where the load’s base was already available in decode and the older memory stage was idle. I’ll test whether issuing those loads from EX gives the structural slot a stronger candidate."}}
