nch DIV/REM\n  from the registered operands, use the four-bit seed and narrow first\n  update while registering 3D, then use two parallel-trial radix-4 digits per\n  update for the remaining six updates. Hold completion until transfer and\n  keep the same ALTOPS schedule and opcode-specific su\n…[3085 of 6157 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:6b6b2d4f071a3096]…\nv\n    description: \"Connect completion and slot availability, exclude late producers from EX/MEM bypass, and retain the current predictor connections and single-channel RVFI port contract.\"\n  - file: rtl/wb_stage.sv\n    description: \"Use the registered architectural value for writeback and bypass. Keep retirement and write enables qualified by validity.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Check independent MUL throughput, MUL-to-store and load-to-MUL dependencies, raw source aliases, and an older stalled request during a younger redirect. Verify stable bus payload, one accepted store, misalignment traps, exact RVFI fields and contiguous order.\"\n  - file: test/test_mul_unit.py\n    description: \"Retain all exact RV32M product vectors and check consecutive low-word inputs, high-word completion and reset.\"\n  - file: test/test_div_unit.py\n    description: \"Retain exact divide and remainder vectors and exercise the 255/256 narrow-update boundary, divisor multiples above 32 bits and held completion.\"\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
