{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_6", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg '\\\"category\\\"\\\\s*:\\\\s*\\\"structural\\\"|hyp-20261121-001-r4s0' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python3 -c 'import json,sys; rows=list(map(json.loads,sys.stdin)); print(list(rows[-1])); [print(json.dumps({k:r[k] for k in r if k.lower() not in (\\\"implementation_notes\\\", \\\"eval_result\\\", \\\"metrics\\\", \\\"timing\\\")} )[:5000]) for r in rows]'\"", "aggregated_output": "['id', 'title', 'category', 'motivation', 'hypothesis', 'expected_impact', 'changes', 'outcome', 'fitness', 'delta_pct', 'vs_baseline', 'fmax_mhz', 'ipc_coremark', 'cycles', 'iterations', 'lut4', 'ff', 'seeds', 'perturbations', 'lutram', 'bsram', 'dsp', 'critical_path', 'logic_levels', 'formal_passed', 'cosim_passed', 'error', 'implementation_notes', 'timestamp', 'slot', 'round_id', 'lesson']\n{\"id\": \"hyp-20261121-002-r1s1\", \"title\": \"Move DIV and REM to a shared iterative execute unit\", \"category\": \"structural\", \"motivation\": \"Bench's baseline closed at 5.442 MHz median Fmax and 12.12 CoreMark\\niterations per second. The reported 199.837 ns, 156-cell path runs from a\\nwriteback destination through forwarding and the EX ALU toward the data\\naddress path. The four combinational division and remainder expressions\\nfeed the same result mux as ordinary ALU operations and are the likely\\nsource of the deep logic. Every instruction pays their timing cost.\\nAn unmodified baseline cosim with both bus stalls enabled reproduced\\nthe logged 4,491,485 bracketed cycles and passed CoreMark CRC validation.\\nIts 2,922,015 timed retirements included zero DIV, DIVU, REM or REMU\\ninstructions.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"Bench's baseline closed at 5.442 MHz median Fmax and 12.12 CoreMark\\niterations per second. The reported 199.837 ns, 156-cell path runs from a\\nwriteback destination through forwarding and the EX ALU toward the data\\naddress path. The four combinational division and remainder expressions\\nfeed the same result mux as ordinary ALU operations and are the likely\\nsource of the deep logic. Every instruction pays their timing cost.\\nAn unmodified baseline cosim with both bus stalls enabled reproduced\\nthe logged 4,491,485 bracketed cycles and passed CoreMark CRC validation.\\nIts 2,922,015 timed retirements included zero DIV, DIVU, REM or REMU\\ninstructions.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": \"Move DIV, DIVU, REM and REMU into one blocking, clocked execute unit. At\\nlaunch, capture forwarded operands and the operation, and register t\n…[22329 of 25401 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:c2e37c98a4d3ecc8]…\nt order within the existing formal window.\\n\\nAllow roughly 40,000 additional cycles for late-result interlocks,\\nbased on the earlier lane's 36,275-cycle increase. At 4.23 million\\ncycles the 4.6% acceptance margin requires about 61.48 MHz. Repeating\\nthe earlier lane's 62.861 MHz would yield about 148.6 iterations/sec.\\nTarget 64 MHz after the address split, yielding about 151.3 iterations/sec\\nor +9%. Measure median Gowin Fmax and stalled CoreMark cycles, check\\nwhether the worst paths move out of the shared EX result logic, and\\nrequire the existing formal, cosim and canonical CRC checks to pass.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 9, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Add a dedicated EX/MEM effective address and a late-result operation with registered operands. Carry the selected architectural write value in MEM/WB.\"}, {\"file\": \"rtl/ex_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Form the memory address in its own forwarded-base plus I/S-immediate adder. Capture the \n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"rg -n -i 'forward|precomput|retim|early operand|bypass' cores/bench/CORE_PHILOSOPHY.md formal/checks_si.cfg tools/tournament.py && sed -n '1,160p' fpga/core_bench_si.sv\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -n -i 'forward|precomput|retim|early operand|bypass' cores/bench/CORE_PHILOSOPHY.md formal/checks_si.cfg tools/tournament.py && sed -n '1,160p' fpga/core_bench_si.sv\"", "aggregated_output": "formal/checks_si.cfg:18:# liveness — CPU makes forward progress under any symbolic stream\n// fpga/core_bench_si.sv\n//\n// FPGA Fmax wrapper for single-issue (`nret 1`) cores. Same shape as\n// core_bench.sv but instantiates `core` with only the channel-0 RVFI port\n// set — no `_1` ports. Selected by the orchestrator (via BENCH env var in\n// synth.tcl) when cores/<target>/core.yaml declares nret: 1.\n//\n// See core_bench.sv for the rationale on LFSR-driven imem, the dmem\n// model, the V2 stall generator, and why the LED observes only the\n// memory-side outputs (RVFI-only logic is pruned).\nmodule core_bench (\n  input  logic clock,\n  input  logic reset,\n  output logic led\n);\n\n  logic [31:0] lfsr;\n  always_ff @(posedge clock or posedge reset)\n    if (reset) lfsr <= 32'h1;\n    else       lfsr <= {lfsr[30:0], lfsr[31] ^ lfsr[21] ^ lfsr[1] ^ lfsr[0]};\n\n  logic [31:0] dmem [0:2047];\n  logic [31:0] dmem_rdata;\n  logic [31:0] dmem_addr;\n  logic [31:0] dmem_wdata;\n  logic [3:0]  dmem_wen;\n  logic        dmem_ren;\n\n  always_ff @(posedge clock) begin\n    if (dmem_wen[0]) dmem[dmem_addr[12:2]][7:0]   <= dmem_wdata[7:0];\n    if (dmem_wen[1]) dmem[dmem_addr[12:2]][15:8]  <= dmem_wdata[15:8];\n    if (dmem_wen[2]) dmem[dmem_addr[12:2]][23:16] <= dmem_wdata[23:16];\n    if (dmem_wen[3]) dmem[dmem_addr[12:2]][31:24] <= dmem_wdata[31:24];\n  end\n  assign dmem_rdata = dmem[dmem_addr[12:2]];\n\n  logic [31:0] imem_addr;\n  // Single-channel RVFI port set (NRET=1 contract). Connected for\n  // elaboration only; nothing observes it, so synthesis prunes it.\n  logic        rvfi_valid_0;\n  logic [63:0] rvfi_order_0;\n  logic [31:0] rvfi_insn_0, rvfi_pc_rdata_0, rvfi_pc_wdata_0;\n  logic [31:0] rvfi_rd_wdata_0, rvfi_rs1_rdata_0, rvfi_rs2_rdata_0;\n  logic [31:0] rvfi_mem_addr_0, rvfi_mem_rdata_0, rvfi_mem_wdata_0;\n  logic [4:0]  rvfi_rs1_addr_0, rvfi_rs2_addr_0, rvfi_rd_addr_0;\n  logic [3:0]  rvfi_mem_rmask_0, rvfi_mem_wmask_0;\n  logic [1:0]  rvfi_mode_0, rvfi_ixl_0;\n  logic        rvfi_trap_0, rvfi_halt_0, rvfi_intr_0;\n\n  // V2: memory-ready signals come from the same stall sequence the\n  // CoreMark simulation uses, so stall-handling logic is part of the\n  // timed netlist (fpga/bench_stall_gen.sv).\n  logic imem_ready, dmem_ready;\n  bench_stall_gen stall_gen (\n    .clock      (clock),\n    .reset      (reset),\n    .imem_ready (imem_ready),\n    .dmem_ready (dmem_ready)\n  );\n\n  core cpu (\n    .clock            (clock),\n    .reset            (reset),\n    .io_imemAddr      (imem_addr),\n    .io_imemData      (lfsr),\n    .io_imemReady     (imem_ready),\n    .io_dmemAddr      (dmem_addr),\n    .io_dmemWData     (dmem_wdata),\n    .io_dmemRData     (dmem_rdata),\n    .io_dmemWEn       (dmem_wen),\n    .io_dmemREn       (dmem_ren),\n    .io_dmemReady     (dmem_ready),\n    .io_rvfi_valid_0    (rvfi_valid_0),\n    .io_rvfi_order_0    (rvfi_order_0),\n    .io_rvfi_insn_0     (rvfi_insn_0),\n    .io_rvfi_trap_0     (rvfi_trap_0),\n    .io_rvfi_halt_0     (rvfi_halt_0),\n    .io_rvfi_intr_0     (rvfi_intr_0),\n    .io_rvfi_mode_0     (rvfi_mode_0),\n    .io_rvfi_ixl_0      (rvfi_ixl_0),\n    .io_rvfi_rs1_addr_0 (rvfi_rs1_addr_0),\n    .io_rvfi_rs1_rdata_0(rvfi_rs1_rdata_0),\n    .io_rvfi_rs2_addr_0 (rvfi_rs2_addr_0),\n    .io_rvfi_rs2_rdata_0(rvfi_rs2_rdata_0),\n    .io_rvfi_rd_addr_0  (rvfi_rd_addr_0),\n    .io_rvfi_rd_wdata_0 (rvfi_rd_wdata_0),\n    .io_rvfi_pc_rdata_0 (rvfi_pc_rdata_0),\n    .io_rvfi_pc_wdata_0 (rvfi_pc_wdata_0),\n    .io_rvfi_mem_addr_0 (rvfi_mem_addr_0),\n    .io_rvfi_mem_rmask_0(rvfi_mem_rmask_0),\n    .io_rvfi_mem_wmask_0(rvfi_mem_wmask_0),\n    .io_rvfi_mem_rdata_0(rvfi_mem_rdata_0),\n    .io_rvfi_mem_wdata_0(rvfi_mem_wdata_0)\n  );\n\n  // V2: observe only the memory-side outputs. Everything the core computes\n  // reaches the fetch address or a store, so the datapath stays in the\n  // netlist; logic that only drives RVFI (a verification port a deployed\n  // core would not have) is pruned and does not count toward Fmax or area.\n  assign led = ^{imem_addr, dmem_addr, dmem_wdata, dmem_wen, dmem_ren, dmem_rdata};\n\nendmodule\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"rg 'hyp-20261121-001-r4s0|hyp-20261121-002-r4s1|hyp-20261121-003-r4s2' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python3 -c 'import json,sys; keys=\\\"id fitness fmax_mhz cycles seeds perturbations critical_path implementation_notes\\\".split(); [print(json.dumps({k:r[k] for k in keys}, indent=2)) for r in map(json.loads,sys.stdin)]'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_8", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg 'hyp-20261121-001-r4s0|hyp-20261121-002-r4s1|hyp-20261121-003-r4s2' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python3 -c 'import json,sys; keys=\\\"id fitness fmax_mhz cycles seeds perturbations critical_path implementation_notes\\\".split(); [print(json.dumps({k:r[k] for k in keys}, indent=2)) for r in map(json.loads,sys.stdin)]'\"", "aggregated_output": "{\n  \"id\": \"hyp-20261121-001-r4s0\",\n  \"fitness\": 154.3,\n  \"fmax_mhz\": 64.657,\n  \"cycles\": 4190307,\n  \"seeds\": [\n    62.587,\n    64.657,\n    64.657\n  ],\n  \"perturbations\": [\n    [\n      0,\n      62.587,\n      17\n    ],\n    [\n      1,\n      64.657,\n      18\n    ],\n    [\n      2,\n      64.657,\n      18\n    ]\n  ],\n  \"critical_path\": {\n    \"from\": \"cpu/u_mem/reg_q.rd_0_s0\",\n    \"to\": \"cpu/u_ex/reg_q.alu_result_21_s0\",\n    \"slack_ns\": -10.978,\n    \"arrival_ns\": 21.272,\n    \"logic_cells\": 34,\n    \"modules\": [\n      \"clock_ibuf\",\n      \"cpu/u_fwd\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\",\n      \"cpu/u_ex\"\n    ]\n  },\n  \"implementation_notes\": \"# Bench EX datapath implementation\\n\\n- EX computes the effective address from forwarded `rs1` and the decoded I- or S-type immediate. The 12-bit sum runs in parallel with three upper-word candidates. EX/MEM holds the full address with the store payload and memory controls through data-bus stalls. MEM uses it for the bus address, alignment, lane masks, load extraction, and aligned RVFI address.\\n- EX ORs five independently masked results for the jump link, low multiply, high multiply, division or remainder, and base ALU. This preserves the forwarding schedule, branch prediction, load-use interlock, and single-cycle low `MUL`.\\n- The two asynchronous register reads share one 32-word distributed RAM array. Reset clears the written bits. Reads retain hardwired `x0` and matching-write priority on both ports.\\n- The divider launches with four seed bits, consumes four more bits with eight-bit restoring arithmetic while registering `3D`, then performs two radix-4 steps on each of six edges. Each radix-4 step compares all three multiples in parallel. The hardware and ALTOPS paths retain the launch-to-completion schedule and hold completion until consumed.\\n\\nJALR also uses the split address adder because it has the same signed 12-bit offset. It still clears target bit zero before redirecting. The existing four-bit divider seed computes the magnitude of its two high bit pairs with independen\n…[8215 of 11287 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:ed009b99b0dd4bef]…\nhed)` passed the second retry. The final timing changes passed the suite again.\\n- All seven cocotb runners passed, including 23 pipeline cases. The directed cases cover loop recovery over an unready bus, full refill, buffered issue during unready fetch, same-index training, last-word parking and full-width out-of-window resolution.\\n- `make cosim TARGET=bench NRET=1` matched the ISS for selftest and three random programs with zero-wait and stalled buses. Stalled CoreMark passed all five canonical CRCs, reported `Correct operation validated.` and performed no out-of-bounds memory access.\\n\\n## CoreMark and Gowin\\n\\n| Gowin placement | Fmax |\\n| --- | ---: |\\n| 0 | 58.706 MHz |\\n| 1 | 59.469 MHz |\\n| 2 | 59.469 MHz |\\n| Median | 59.469 MHz |\\n\\n`make fpga TARGET=bench NRET=1` reproduced all three placement results. The 10-iteration run took 3,956,704 marker-bracketed cycles with both stalls enabled, down 5.57% from the champion. The median gives **150.30 iterations/s**, up 8.18% from 138.94 iterations/s.\\n\"\n}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
