{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_3", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c 'cat cores/bench/LESSONS.md schemas/hypothesis.schema.json'", "aggregated_output": "- 2026-11-21 hyp-20261121-001-r1s0 (improvement, +785.40%): Rare operations on the shared EX forwarding path can limit the clock for every instruction, so moving DIV/REM into a shared iterative divider raised median Gowin Fmax from 5.442 to 48.196 MHz with unchanged CoreMark timed cycles because no DIV/REM retired between the timing markers.\n- 2026-11-21 hyp-20261121-002-r1s1 (regression, +733.33%): Saving one DIV/REM cycle with three cascaded radix-4 steps per clock left CoreMark at 4,491,485 timed cycles, so the radix-4 design lost on median Gowin Fmax (45.366 versus 48.196 MHz for radix-2), with its clock limited by the register-file-to-fetch-PC path through EX and hazard logic.\n- 2026-11-21 hyp-20261121-003-r1s2 (regression, +9.08%): Benchmark fetch predictors on the current champion RTL because the single-read tagged BTB saved 6.79% of CoreMark timed cycles by avoiding taken-transfer bubbles, a gain outweighed by the older combinational DIV/REM ALU limiting median Fmax to 5.533 MHz against the iterative-divider champion’s 48.196 MHz.\n- 2026-11-21 hyp-20261121-001-r2s0 (improvement, +13.61%): Registered high-product correction, a parallelized four-bit divider seed, and wrong-path squashes via ID/EX validity shortened EX arithmetic and redirect-to-load-use feedback paths, raising median Gowin Fmax from 48.196 to 54.759 MHz while keeping CoreMark’s hot MUL single-cycle and preserving its timed cycle count.\n- 2026-11-21 hyp-20261121-002-r2s1 (regression, +7.49%): The two-entry fetch FIFO with decode-stage JAL and operand-ready BEQ/BNE redirects cut stalled CoreMark cycles by 6.59%, with divider feedback capping median Gowin Fmax at 48.391 MHz against the 51.15 MHz needed to match the EX-tuned champion.\n- 2026-11-21 hyp-20261121-003-r2s2 (regression, +8.73%): The forwarded ALU path limited the tagged BTB with parallel EX successor checks to 48.845 MHz median Gowin Fmax, below the 51.04 MHz needed to match the round’s EX-tuned winner after a 6.79% cut in stalled CoreMark cycles.\n- 2026-11-21 hyp-20261121-001-r3s0 \n…[3464 of 6536 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:82536732bfd48bc8]…\nnLength\": 5},\n    \"category\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"micro_opt\",\"structural\",\"extension\",\"predictor\",\"memory\"]},\n    \"motivation\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"hypothesis\":  {\"type\": \"string\", \"minLength\": 20},\n    \"expected_impact\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"required\": [\"fitness_delta_pct\",\"confidence\"],\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"fitness_delta_pct\": {\"type\": \"integer\"},\n        \"confidence\": {\"type\": \"string\", \"enum\": [\"low\",\"medium\",\"high\"]}\n      }\n    },\n    \"changes\": {\n      \"type\": \"array\", \"minItems\": 1,\n      \"items\": {\n        \"type\": \"object\",\n        \"required\": [\"file\",\"description\"],\n        \"properties\": {\n          \"file\":        {\n            \"type\": \"string\",\n            \"description\": \"Must be under rtl/ (any extension) or be a test/test_*.py cocotb suite. Anything else is rejected by the runtime sandbox check.\",\n            \"pattern\": \"^(rtl/[^.].*|test/test_[^/]+\\\\.py)$\"\n          },\n          \"description\": {\"type\": \"string\"}\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
