{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_4", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg '\\\"category\\\"\\\\s*:\\\\s*\\\"structural\\\"' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python3 -c 'import json,sys\nfor line in sys.stdin:\n d=json.loads(line)\n h=d.get(\\\"hypothesis\\\",{})\n if isinstance(h,dict):\n  print({k:v for k,v in d.items() if k in (\\\"id\\\",\\\"status\\\",\\\"outcome\\\",\\\"fitness\\\",\\\"fmax_mhz\\\",\\\"coremark_iter_s\\\")})\n  print(h.get(\\\"id\\\"),h.get(\\\"title\\\"),h.get(\\\"hypothesis\\\"))\n else:\n  print(str(d)[:280])\n'\"", "aggregated_output": "{'id': 'hyp-20261121-002-r1s1', 'outcome': 'regression', 'fitness': 101.0, 'fmax_mhz': 45.366}\nNone None Move DIV, DIVU, REM and REMU into one blocking, clocked execute unit. At\nlaunch, capture forwarded operands and the operation, and register the\noperand magnitudes and sign flags. On the first update clock, compute\nthe top radix-4 digit from the dividend magnitude's top two bits and\nregister the divisor multiples D, 2D and 3D. Among nonzero divisors,\nonly magnitudes one, two and three can yield a nonzero first digit. On\neach of the next five clocks, cascade three radix-4 digit steps to\nconsume the remaining 30 bits. A step appends two dividend bits to the\npartial remainder and uses three parallel trial subtractions to select\nthe largest multiple that fits. Use 34-bit divisor multiples and 35-bit\nsubtracts to preserve the full trial value and detect borrow. Select\nthe quotient or remainder, apply its sign and handle divisor zero and\nsigned overflow before the existing EX/MEM transfer. Keep the result\nstable until that transfer.\nThis adds seven cycles with ready buses, leaving margin in the existing\nten-cycle liveness window for a redirect or load-use bubble. Use the same\nissue and completion schedule for ALTOPS, with the four existing\nopcode-specific arithmetic substitutes.\n\nHold fetch and ID/EX for the divide, allow older MEM/WB work to drain, and\ninject bubbles into EX/MEM until result transfer. Give an older blocked\ndata request priority over divider launch and EX/MEM writes. Snapshot\nthe forwarded source values for RVFI so draining the pipeline cannot\nchange the reported operands. On transfer, send the result through the\nexisting result forwarding and single-channel retirement path exactly\nonce. Reset cancels any pending divide. Ordinary instructions retain\ntheir existing execute latency, and loads and stores retain their bus\nhandshake and alignment rules.\n\nThe registered recurrence should remove the full-width combinational\ndivider from the ordinary execute path and reduce LUT pressure. The\nmeasured instruc\n…[11091 of 14163 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:540baf9df2c58498]…\nss slots drain. Keep the same ALTOPS schedule, one-cycle low MUL,\nbus handshakes, branch predictor and single-channel RVFI behavior.\n\nThe scratch implementation with final selects registered reached\n72.664, 80.065 and 80.065 MHz across the three Gowin placements and\npassed canonical CoreMark CRC validation in 4,190,307 timed cycles.\nThe median gives 191.07 iter/sec, up 23.8% from the champion. Placement\nzero used 3,596 logic cells and 816 registers. Its worst path runs from\nthe registered WB value to the divider launch seed. Placements one and\ntwo are limited by the divider recurrence. At the measured cycle count,\nabout 67.63 MHz clears the acceptance margin.\n\nThe scratch build passed all 53 single-channel ALTOPS formal checks,\nall seven cocotb suites, and the standard cosim gate. Directed tests\nalso checked a double destination match, bypass fallback after a\nmisaligned link or load, and a held consumer of a load behind a stalled\nstore. Repeat the three placements and correctness gates after implementation.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
