{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_8", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg '\\\"id\\\": \\\"hyp-20261121-003-r[6789]s2\\\"' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python3 -c 'import sys,json; rs=map(json.loads,sys.stdin); [(print(r[\\\"id\\\"],r[\\\"outcome\\\"], {k:v for k,v in r.items() if k in [\\\"error\\\",\\\"fitness\\\",\\\"formal_passed\\\",\\\"cosim_passed\\\"]}), print(r[\\\"hypothesis\\\"][\\\"hypothesis\\\"]), print(r.get(\\\"implementation_notes\\\",\\\"\\\"))) for r in rs]'\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261121-003-r6s2 regression {'fitness': 182.82, 'formal_passed': True, 'cosim_passed': True, 'error': None}\nAttach a loop stream buffer to the predicted fetch producer. Train one\nloop descriptor from an advancing, aligned, taken backward conditional\nbranch whose inclusive body spans at most 128 words in the 1 MiB\ninstruction window. Register the event separately from the unconditionally\ncaptured EX target and branch PC so the branch condition only drives\nthe training-valid bit. Keep the current descriptor on an inner\nbackedge fully contained in its range. Stage a refill when a ready bus word\nmatches the producer PC, then write only aligned words in the tracked\nloop that precede the last mapped word. Clear word validity on\nallocation, so the seven low word-PC bits uniquely index the current\nloop. Qualify a replay with the full upper address, the stored page bit\nthat distinguishes two adjacent 512-byte pages, and per-word validity.\n\nStore each instruction, page bit, and the precomputed 18-bit word\ntarget and target eligibility bit in synchronous block RAM. Read the\nRAM at the computed next producer index on the same edge that captures\nthe next producer PC. Treat a same-index read/write collision as a\nmiss for the following cycle. Use the existing folded direction table\nfor both sources and select between the bus target, the replay target\nand fall-through in parallel. Compute the bus target with a 19-bit\nword-address sum whose high bit detects targets outside the window for\nan in-window source. Carry the PC, word and prediction bit through\na three-entry distributed RAM fall-through queue. Form the full\narchitectural direct target in EX from the registered PC and immediate.\n\nGive a ready, matching bus word priority and substitute a replay hit\nwhen it is unavailable. When replay advances over an unready bus,\nlatch the outstanding request address until ready. Discard its stale\nresponse and present the current producer PC on the following cycle.\nRegistered EX recovery supersedes the held request, discards queued\nwr\n…[24841 of 27913 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:29a45e37ed141456]…\n link, memory and\nsingle-channel RVFI behavior.\n\nA trace model covered 1.60 million of 2.92 million timed retirements with\nfour entries, compared with 1.04 million with one. Both modeled the\nheader as a bus fetch and delayed use by five retirements after publication.\nA cycle-level Verilator proxy supplied the recorded direction and made\nmatching warm words available to the champion FIFO during imem stalls.\nIt reproduced 3,956,104 cycles with the proxy disabled and ran in\n3,662,345 cycles with replay and a five-cycle publication delay, a 7.43%\nreduction with canonical CRCs. The proxy assumes a replay word is ready\nwhenever the FIFO can admit it. FPGA timing remains unmeasured. At an\nimplementation target of 3.70 million timed cycles and 88.5 MHz,\nfitness would be 239.19 iter/sec, up 6.1%. At that cycle count the median\nneeds to exceed 87.27 MHz to clear the acceptance margin. Measure the\nactual bracketed cycles and median of the three Gowin placements, and\ncheck the canonical CRCs and existing formal gates.\n\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
