producer PC, before the recovery and held-bus address muxes. Select\n  the replay instruction and successor with the one-hot matches. Give\n  the matching ready bus word priority and keep its empty-queue bypass.\n  Replay always enqueues into the five-entry queue. Select its successor\n  from PC+4 and the recorded direct\n…[2023 of 5095 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:63a46cbae6332374]…\nments and run the unmodified\n  formal and stalled RVFI checks on the implementation.\nexpected_impact:\n  fitness_delta_pct: 8\n  confidence: medium\nchanges:\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Add synchronous PC+8 prediction replay and four persistent PC-tagged response slots. Sweep the RAM through its fill port on reset and FENCE.I. Isolate slot writes from queue advance, indirect recovery and stale bus handshakes.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Export FENCE.I on architectural advance and use sequential recovery for it. Continue resolving replayed predictions and reporting the actual RVFI successor.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Route the advancing FENCE.I event into fetch for replay invalidation.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Check persistent tagged replay through holds and redirects, lookup aliases, stale request disposal, and progress and code visibility during and after FENCE.I invalidation. Check ordered retirement and absent wrong-path side effects.\"\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
