kly\\ntaken and strengthen or weaken matching entries on outcomes. Install legal\\naligned jumps as strongly taken. Train once per advancing valid EX control\\ninstruction and suppress training for traps. Reset the valid bits and leave\\nthe payload arrays unreset to allow distributed RAM inference.\\n\\nUse only the fetch-indexed table read. On an accepted fetch, register that\\ninstruction's lookup hit and counter alongside the IF PC update for use by\\nEX training on\n…[32127 of 35199 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:53ce4c78b392e4e4]…\nTL.\\n- `make cosim TARGET=bench NRET=1` passed selftest and all three random programs with and without bus stalls. CoreMark passed the canonical CRC checks with both stalls enabled.\\n- `make fpga TARGET=bench NRET=1` passed the timing-marker checks and measured 4,186,330 bracketed cycles for ten iterations with both stalls enabled. Gowin placement options 0, 1, and 2 reached 46.456, 48.845, and 48.845 MHz. The 48.845 MHz median gives 116.68 iterations/sec, 8.73% above 107.31.\\n- Option 0 used 3,037 logic cells and 12 LUT RAMs. The logic cell count grew 14.0% from the champion. The worst setup paths traverse the forwarded ALU datapath.\\n\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-21T14:02:23.819544Z\",\n  \"slot\": 2,\n  \"round_id\": 2,\n  \"lesson\": \"- 2026-11-21 hyp-20261121-003-r2s2 (regression, +8.73%): The forwarded ALU path limited the tagged BTB with parallel EX successor checks to 48.845 MHz median Gowin Fmax, below the 51.04 MHz needed to match the round\\u2019s EX-tuned winner after a 6.79% cut in stalled CoreMark cycles.\"\n}\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
