{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"rg -n '\\\"category\\\"[[:space:]]*:[[:space:]]*\\\"predictor\\\"|hyp-20261121-003-r3s2' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | cut -c 1-700 && head -c 700 cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl && git log -5 --oneline\"","aggregated_output":"4:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261121-003-r1s2\", \"title\": \"Predict hot control transfers with a single-read tagged target buffer\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The bench core fetches fall-through until EX resolves a control transfer. Each\\naligned taken branch or jump normally discards one fetch opportunity because\\nIF feeds ID/EX without a separate IF/ID register. CoreMark repeatedly visits\\nloop branches, calls, and returns. The baseline's 5.442 MHz median Fmax is\\nlimited by the forwarded ALU path, so the predictor must earn its gain in\\nmarker-bracketed cycles while keeping the fetch feedback path short.\\n\", \"hypothesis\": {\"motivation\": \"The bench core fetches fall-through until EX resolves \n7:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261121-003-r2s2\", \"title\": \"Predict hot transfers with a tagged BTB and parallel recovery checks\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The current bench champion loses one fetch slot on each aligned taken\\nbranch or jump because IF feeds ID/EX directly and resolves transfers in EX.\\nThe round-one 64-entry BTB reduced marker-bracketed CoreMark cycles from\\n4,491,485 to 4,186,330 with both bus stalls enabled. Its Fmax was measured\\non the older combinational-divider core. The iterative-divider champion\\nreaches 48.196 MHz, and the other divider trial exposed an EX-to-fetch\\ntiming path. Preserving that clock while removing taken-transfer bubbles\\nis the opportunity for this\n10:{\"id\": \"hyp-20261121-003-r3s2\", \"title\": \"Predict direct transfers with a direction-only fetch table\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The current champion runs ten timed CoreMark iterations in 4,491,485 cycles\\nat 54.759 MHz. The tagged BTB trial on the round-two starting RTL saved\\n6.79% of cycles and scored 116.68 iter/sec at a 48.845 MHz median. The\\ncurrent champion scores 121.92 iter/sec. The bench pipeline has no IF/ID\\nregister, so predicting a direct transfer at fetch acceptance can still put\\nthe target in front of EX on the next cycle. Deriving that target from the\\nfetched instruction lets EX verify direction with one bit and removes the\\ntarget RAM and full-address ma\n{\"id\": \"baseline-bench-29c86c4\", \"title\": \"Baseline retest for cores/bench\", \"category\": \"micro_opt\", \"outcome\": \"improvement\", \"fitness\": 12.12, \"delta_pct\": 0.0, \"vs_baseline\": 0.0, \"fmax_mhz\": 5.442, \"ipc_coremark\": 2e-06, \"cycles\": 4491485, \"iterations\": 10, \"lut4\": 12312, \"ff\": 460, \"seeds\": [5.14, 5.442, 5.442], \"perturbations\": [[0, 5.14, 150], [1, 5.442, 149], [2, 5.442, 149]], \"lutram\": 8, \"bsram\": 6, \"dsp\": 6, \"critical_path\": {\"from\": \"cpu/u_mem/reg_q.rd_3_s0\", \"to\": \"dmem_0_dmem_0_0_0_s\", \"slack_ns\": -189.542, \"arrival_ns\": 199.837, \"logic_cells\": 156, \"modules\": [\"clock_ibuf\", \"cpu/u_fwd\", \"cpu/u_ex\", \"cpu/u_ex/u_alu\", \"cpu/u_ex\"]}, \"logic_levels\": 150, \"formal_passed\": true, \"ca957b3b log: hyp-20261121-003-r3s2 improvement\n42e3e64 log: hyp-20261121-002-r3s1 regression\nd9e02f8 log: hyp-20261121-001-r3s0 regression\n8d6dfab hyp-20261121-003-r3s2: Predict direct transfers with a direction-only fetch table (+14.0%)\n67483f5 log: hyp-20261121-003-r2s2 regression\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
