n EX from the registered PC and decoded immediate, in\nparallel with operand forwarding and the branch comparison. Use the\nimmediate's bit 1 to check direct-transfer alignment since the PC is word\naligned. Keep the one-bit mismatch check and derive the authoritative RVFI\nnext PC from the architectural resolution.\n\nIF only needs to form an aligned in-window target. For a source PC in\nthe 1 MiB window, add its zero-extended 18-bit word index to the signed\n19-bit B/J word offset in 19 bits. A clear result bit 18 certifies the\ntarget is in range. Use the offset's halfword bit to qualify alignment.\nOutsi\n…[16416 of 19488 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:13201eb3435db694]…\ned\nrecovery path. Preserve the existing trap and link semantics,\nmemory-side handshakes and single-channel resolved RVFI next PC.\n\nA scratch prototype on the current champion passed stalled CoreMark\nwith all canonical CRCs and no out-of-bounds access. It took\n3,956,104 marker-bracketed cycles, a 5.59% saving. Gowin placement\noptions 0, 1, and 2 measured 67.492, 67.274, and 67.274 MHz. The\nmedian scores 170.05 iter/sec, 10.21% above the champion. This cycle\ncount requires a median above 63.85 MHz to clear the 4.6% threshold.\nThe median placement's worst path ran from MEM/WB forwarding to\nthe divider seed. Placement 0 used 3,964 reported logic cells and\n1,352 registers.\n\nThe scratch prototype passed all 53 single-channel ALTOPS formal\nchecks and matched the ISS on selftest and all three random\nprograms with zero-wait and stalled buses. All seven cocotb\nrunners passed after updating the loop-exit request trace for\nrunahead and adding queue fill, buffered issue, held JALR\nrecovery, and last-word parking cases.\n\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
