e field, compare in ID against the current EX and MEM destinations. Choose the youngest eligible nonzero writer and register a one-hot choice among the upcoming EX/MEM value, upcoming MEM/WB value, and captured register-file value. Qualify an EX link writer with its target alignment and a MEM load writer with its access alignment before choosing, so an older eligible match can supply the value if the younger instructio\n…[18774 of 21846 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:1087ce3b6002e7d3]…\nclose in placements 1 and 2.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Verilator lint passed in hardware and ALTOPS modes. All seven cocotb suites passed, covering 88 cases.\n- `NRET=1 make cosim TARGET=bench` matched the ISS on selftest and all three random programs with ready buses and with both stall generators enabled. Stalled CoreMark reported `Correct operation validated.` and matched all five canonical CRCs (`e9f5`, `e714`, `1fd7`, `8e3a`, `fcaf`).\n- `bash formal/run_all.sh` passed all 53 single-channel ALTOPS checks on the retimed RTL, with zero failures or retries. This includes forward-PC consistency, register consistency, and liveness.\n\ntimestamp 2026-11-21T16:47:09.004133Z\nslot 2\nround_id 6\nlesson - 2026-11-21 hyp-20261121-003-r6s2 (regression, +8.23%): Resolved-backedge replay hid imem stalls and cut timed CoreMark cycles by 7.74%, with the predicted fetch PC path through decode admission to last-word parking capping median Gowin Fmax at 66.730 MHz, below the 70.38 MHz needed to match the divider-retimed round winner.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
