{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_10", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg '\\\"category\\\"\\\\s*:\\\\s*\\\"predictor\\\"' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python -c 'import sys,json; [(print(r[\\\"id\\\"],r[\\\"title\\\"],r[\\\"cycles\\\"],r[\\\"fmax_mhz\\\"]),print(r[\\\"hypothesis\\\"][\\\"hypothesis\\\"]) if r[\\\"id\\\"].endswith((\\\"r6s2\\\",\\\"r7s2\\\",\\\"r8s2\\\")) else None) for r in map(json.loads,sys.stdin)]'\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261121-003-r1s2 Predict hot control transfers with a single-read tagged target buffer 4186330 5.533\nhyp-20261121-003-r2s2 Predict hot transfers with a tagged BTB and parallel recovery checks 4186330 48.845\nhyp-20261121-003-r3s2 Predict direct transfers with a direction-only fetch table 4190307 58.22\nhyp-20261121-003-r4s2 Run the branch predictor ahead of decode through a compact fetch queue 3956704 59.469\nhyp-20261121-003-r5s2 Decouple predicted fetch with a five-entry queue and registered recovery 3956104 66.827\nhyp-20261121-003-r6s2 Replay short instruction loops selected by resolved backedges 3650094 66.73\nAttach a loop stream buffer to the predicted fetch producer. Train one\nloop descriptor from an advancing, aligned, taken backward conditional\nbranch whose inclusive body spans at most 128 words in the 1 MiB\ninstruction window. Register the event separately from the unconditionally\ncaptured EX target and branch PC so the branch condition only drives\nthe training-valid bit. Keep the current descriptor on an inner\nbackedge fully contained in its range. Stage a refill when a ready bus word\nmatches the producer PC, then write only aligned words in the tracked\nloop that precede the last mapped word. Clear word validity on\nallocation, so the seven low word-PC bits uniquely index the current\nloop. Qualify a replay with the full upper address, the stored page bit\nthat distinguishes two adjacent 512-byte pages, and per-word validity.\n\nStore each instruction, page bit, and the precomputed 18-bit word\ntarget and target eligibility bit in synchronous block RAM. Read the\nRAM at the computed next producer index on the same edge that captures\nthe next producer PC. Treat a same-index read/write collision as a\nmiss for the following cycle. Use the existing folded direction table\nfor both sources and select between the bus target, the replay target\nand fall-through in parallel. Compute the bus target with a 19-bit\nword-address sum whose high bit detects targets outside the window for\nan in-window source. Carry the PC, wo\n…[8212 of 11284 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:8af6f2556beec295]…\ns can start from that word's successor candidates.\n\nKeep the five-entry fall-through queue. Accept the last mapped word\nthrough the queue once, mark it and park on bus acceptance. Exclude it\nfrom replay and let the advancing marked instruction restart fetch at\nits resolved successor. An older recovery clears the hold and squashes\nits marker. Clear replay validity and staged refills on an accepted\noverlapping store. On advancing FENCE.I, invalidate replay and recover\nto PC+4 so younger buffered instructions are discarded. Retain the\narchitectural trap, link, memory and single-channel RVFI behavior.\n\nAt the prior replay cycle count the median must exceed 80.96 MHz to\nclear the 4.6% acceptance margin. An 83 MHz median and 3,651,216 cycles\nwould yield 227.32 iter/sec, a 7.24% gain. The estimate depends on\nretaining replay coverage and the replicated RAM fitting the clock.\nMeasure bracketed cycles, canonical CRCs and Gowin placement options\n0, 1 and 2. Run the RVFI and liveness gates with the existing contracts.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
