uccessor word PC and direct-taken bit. The terminal successor\n  is the header. Warm entries remain available across loop exits.\n\n  Enter replay on ordinary bus acceptance of a matching header PC and\n  instruction. Match the normal PC register against the directory in\n  parall\n…[3467 of 6539 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:c81953034ac4936c]…\nr startup and handle replacement, read credits and invalidation.\"\n  - file: rtl/if_stage.sv\n    description: \"Enter replay at a verified accepted bus header, admit registered replay records through the existing fetch queue, and restore normal bus fetch on recovery or invalidation. Preserve boundary parking and ready handshakes.\"\n  - file: rtl/ex_stage.sv\n    description: \"Export advancing EX instruction, PC and resolved control metadata for trace capture. Force sequential recovery on advancing FENCE.I while keeping resolved RVFI successors and the current direction check.\"\n  - file: rtl/core.sv\n    description: \"Connect trace capture and invalidation to the existing EX advance and accepted store handshakes.\"\n  - file: test/test_pipeline.py\n    description: \"Verify warm entry with a divide immediately after the header, replay through imem stalls and queue holds, interior direction changes and loop exits, and code replacement after a store and FENCE.I. Check retirement PCs, order, and wrong-path side effects.\"\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
