with parallel EX successor checks to 48.845 MHz median Gowin Fmax, below the 51.04 MHz needed to match the round’s EX-tuned winner after a 6.79% cut in stalled CoreMark cycles.\n- 2026-11-21 hyp-20261121-001-r3s0 \n…[9537 of 12609 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:2cd6f6715857191b]…\n direction and alignment in parallel with target carry shifted the setup limit from the queue prediction bit to the queue occupancy path through load-use hazard logic, capping median Gowin Fmax at 86.007 MHz with unchanged CoreMark cycles.\n- 2026-11-21 hyp-20261121-002-r12s1 (regression, +0.31%): A fixed fetch queue head and parallel head and bus load-use comparisons remove the rotating read mux from issue feedback while preserving CoreMark’s 3,558,019 timed cycles, leaving fetch recovery into the producer PC and EX ALU result feedback among the longest paths at 90.263 MHz median Gowin Fmax, below the 94.12 MHz acceptance threshold.\n- 2026-11-21 hyp-20261121-003-r12s2 (regression, +0.90%): Registered parity banks replayed the first two predicted B/J target words with PC+4 predictions, covering instruction-bus stalls missed by sequential PC+8 lookahead and cutting stalled CoreMark cycles by 1.92%, while EX forwarding through the ALU result path capped median Gowin Fmax at 89.052 MHz against the 93 MHz target.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
