_addr_31_s0 19\nhyp-20261121-001-r9s0 Share the EX address adder after simplifying divider staging improvement 93.81 3956104 237.13 cpu/u_id/reg_q.rs1_sel_0_s0 cpu/u_if/select_indirect_q_s0 37\nhyp-20261121-001-r10s0 Bypass load data directly into equality branch resolution regression 87.735 3844873 228.19 cpu/u_mem/reg_q.write_value_9_s0 cpu/u_id/reg_q.valid_s0 32\nhyp-20261121-001-r11s0 Prequalify EX recovery before reducing branch comparisons regression 89.456 3956104 226.12 cpu/u_id/reg_q.pc_2_s0 cpu/u_if/recovery_sequential_in_window_q_s0 12\nhyp-20261121-001-r12s0 Register fetch successor candidates before choosing the next PC regression 86.007 3558019 241.73 cpu/u_if/recovery_pending_q_s0 cpu/u_if/occupancy_q_2_s0 14\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_7", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg 'hyp-20261121-00[123]-r(11|12)s' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python3 -c 'import json,sys; \nfor l in sys.stdin:\n d=json.loads(l); print(d[\\\"id\\\"], d[\\\"category\\\"],d[\\\"fitness\\\"],d[\\\"seeds\\\"],d[\\\"critical_path\\\"]); print(d[\\\"implementation_notes\\\"][:15000])'\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261121-001-r11s0 micro_opt 226.12 [72.883, 89.456, 89.456] {'from': 'cpu/u_id/reg_q.pc_2_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_if/recovery_sequential_in_window_q_s0', 'slack_ns': -8.721, 'arrival_ns': 19.015, 'logic_cells': 12, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_if']}\n# Bench branch recovery\n\nID registers correction qualifiers from the validated transfer class, the issued prediction, the mapped-edge marker, and direct displacement bit 1. Aligned branches carry separate direct and sequential requests for the two outcomes. At the mapped edge, a misaligned direct transfer uses the unconditional sequential request because either branch outcome resumes at PC+4. JALR resolves separately using the forwarded two-bit address sum.\n\nEX compares eight four-bit groups in parallel and combines adjacent groups by passing the lower group's ordering through only when the higher group matches. It uses the sign bits to resolve signed ordering when the signs differ and uses funct3 to choose and invert the condition. The three advancing recovery requests feed the existing IF selectors. Their union squashes ID on the same edge. EX still computes full-width PC+4 and B/J targets, and IF uses the EX/MEM address for JALR.\n\nID also qualifies misaligned JAL link suppression. EX calculates bit 1 of the JALR address sum for each forwarding source in parallel and selects it with the registered operand mask.\n\nThe predictor keeps branch and JAL predictions in separate queue bits and folds the PC candidates before selecting the table index. It registers both possible saturating counter updates beside the branch outcome. The chosen pending value still feeds both lookups on an index alias, and a taken misaligned branch suppresses both forwarding and the table write.\n\nDirected pipeline tests exercise forwarded operands across all comparison groups, both misprediction directions, mapped-edge traps and fall-through, predictor aliasing after a misaligned taken branch, and both bus stalls during recovery.\n\n## Local verification\n\n- Strict Verilator lint and \n…[13049 of 16121 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:d1499eae98c81b9c]…\n Local verification\n\n- Verilator lint and all seven cocotb runners passed.\n- Cosim passed for selftest and all three random traces with and without stalls. Stalled CoreMark passed its canonical CRCs and completed in 3,489,822 cycles between the MMIO markers, 1.92% below the champion.\n- Gowin placement options 0, 1, and 2 reached 87.528, 89.052, and 89.052 MHz. The 89.052 MHz median yields 255.18 CoreMark iterations/sec, up 0.90%. It falls below the 93 MHz target. The two median placements were limited by forwarded EX operands through the ALU result path. Later trials with a split direction table or shared right shifter reduced median Fmax, so the worktree contains the higher-scoring build.\n- Formal passed 52 of 53 checks under the unchanged single-retirement configuration. `reg_ch0` was still solving at the local wall-clock limit without a counterexample. The first run stopped at elaboration because Yosys rejected `$bits` applied to a typedef. Applying `$bits` to the packed record signal resolved the error.\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"rg -i 'false.dep|source.use|load.use|hazard|carry.select' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python3 -c 'import json,sys,re; \nfor l in sys.stdin:\n d=json.loads(l); n=d.get(\\\"implementation_notes\\\",\\\"\\\") or \\\"\\\"; ls=[x.strip() for x in n.splitlines() if re.search(\\\"false.dep|source.use|load.use|carry.select|queue occupancy\\\",x,re.I)]; \n if ls: print(d[\\\"id\\\"],d[\\\"category\\\"],d[\\\"fitness\\\"]); print(\\\"\\\\n\\\".join(x[:650] for x in ls[:6]))'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_9", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"rg -i 'false.dep|source.use|load.use|hazard|carry.select' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python3 -c 'import json,sys,re; \nfor l in sys.stdin:\n d=json.loads(l); n=d.get(\\\"implementation_notes\\\",\\\"\\\") or \\\"\\\"; ls=[x.strip() for x in n.splitlines() if re.search(\\\"false.dep|source.use|load.use|carry.select|queue occupancy\\\",x,re.I)]; \n if ls: print(d[\\\"id\\\"],d[\\\"category\\\"],d[\\\"fitness\\\"]); print(\\\"\\\\n\\\".join(x[:650] for x in ls[:6]))'\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261121-001-r2s0 micro_opt 121.92\nFetch passes the raw instruction and readiness to decode. Redirect and load-use squashes clear ID/EX validity on capture. Load-use detection requires both a valid EX load and ready fetch data. Redirect retains priority over PC holds. Invalid EX entries cannot redirect, launch arithmetic, or pass memory or register-write controls downstream. The top-level memory ports and single-channel RVFI contract are preserved.\nhyp-20261121-002-r2s1 structural 115.35\nAn issuing JAL or taken BEQ/BNE can redirect fetch from ID when its target is aligned. BEQ/BNE use the write-first register-file values when neither source has a pending nonzero writer in EX or MEM. The early target adder uses a B- or J-format offset. The issued instruction carries a bit into EX to suppress a second fetch redirect. EX computes the architectural next PC, link value, and misalignment trap, and handles the remaining transfers. A second bit in EX records a redirect sent while data backpressure holds that entry. EX redirects take priority over ID issue, and load-use bubbles leave the queued instruction available for the next cycle\n- All 78 cocotb cases passed across six suites. Directed pipeline tests covered queue fill and ordered drain under both bus stalls, load-use interlocks, early JAL link forwarding, BEQ/BNE decisions and operand fallback, wrong-path discard, alignment traps, and the instruction-window boundary. A JALR held behind a blocked store redirected once, with one accepted store and exact RVFI PCs and order.\nhyp-20261121-003-r3s2 predictor 138.94\n- The hazard unit uses independent combinational assignments for the dmem hold and younger squash. This keeps the EX hold independent of the raw fetch and load-use logic. The directed pipeline tests check fetch addresses, retirement PCs, link values, traps, and wrong-path effects for cold JAL, trained branches, loop exit under both bus stalls, aliased training, and the negative untaken target at PC zero.\nhyp-20261121-001-r4s0 micro_opt 154.3\n- EX ORs five i\n…[4184 of 7256 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:5ebbc84fa28d4f62]…\nructural 253.69\nThe load-use interlock compares the EX load destination with both raw source fields of the head and both raw bus fields in parallel. Effective head occupancy and bypass validity qualify the comparisons. Registered recovery clears the logical queue and restarts its tail pointers. The corrected response can bypass immediately or populate the fresh head during an issue hold. Replay, stale responses, boundary parking, and FENCE.I retain their original admission rules.\nThe implementation also separates producer PC selection from the acceptance enable. ID zeros unused fallback operands before EX, EX compares branch operands in two halves, and low-word MUL captures the DSP result separately from the ordinary EX/MEM result. These changes improved the queue-only median of 89.629 MHz while preserving instruction and arithmetic latencies. Directed tests check a pop from full, concurrent promotion and append, a buffered load-use hold, and ready and stalled corrections with wrong-path stores in the queue.\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
