 stalled responses with stale data, wrong-path stores, divides and load producers, boundary recovery, and predictor aliasing and alignment.\n\n## Timing changes\n\n- IF selects prehashed fetch indices in parallel with the fetch address. The ordinary branch comparator shares the magnitude comparison between signed and unsigned branches.\n- EX registers memory alignment using the same low address sum that qualifies load-branch issue. EX uses one parallel result selection for ALU, link, multiply, and divide results. MEM recognizes divide retirement from its registered divide tag and validity since a divide issues no memory request.\n\n## Local verification\n\n- An intermediate timing revision failed the BEQ and BNE formal checks when an untaken load-dependent branch had a misaligned target. The ordinary comparator could still see the old source and mark the branch trapped. The revised RTL qualifies the ordinary trap with the branch mode and uses the registered load outcome for the late trap and RVFI successor. A directed regression also checks the predictor entry after each outcome.\n- Strict Verilator lint and single-channel cosimulation passed. Cosimulation covered selftest in ready and stalled modes and canonical CoreMark CRC validation with instruction and data stalls.\n- All seven cocotb suites passed. Stalled CoreMark completed ten iterations in 3,844,873 marker-bracketed cycles, down from 3,956,104 cycles.\n- Final formal run has passed 51 of 53 checks, including BEQ, BNE and liveness. Register consistency and forward-PC consistency are still running.\n- Gowin placement 0 measured 85.723 MHz. Its worst path starts at MEM/WB forwarding and ends at ID/EX validity. Placements 1 and 2 are still running.\n\n{'from': 'cpu/u_mem/reg_q.write_value_9_s0', 'to': 'cpu/u_id/reg_q.valid_s0', 'slack_ns': -6.665, 'arrival_ns': 16.96, 'logic_cells': 32, 'modules': ['clock_ibuf', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_id', 'cpu/u_ex', 'cpu/u_id']}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
