{"type": "item.completed", "item": {"id": "item_70", "type": "command_execution", "command": "/bin/bash -c \"python - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfor l in Path('cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl').read_text().splitlines():\n r=json.loads(l)\n if any(x in r['id'] for x in ('r12s0','r12s1','r13s2')):\n  print(r['id'],r['hypothesis']['hypothesis'], r['implementation_notes'])\nPY\"", "aggregated_output": "hyp-20261121-001-r12s0 Hold the normal producer's low 18 word-address bits in two registers.\nOne captures the direct-target candidate and the other captures the\nsequential or retained-address candidate. Register a single bit that\nchooses the target for an accepted taken prediction. The target\nregister takes the bus B/J sum or the existing replay target according\nto the accepted source, independently of taken direction. The other\nregister takes the accepted bus or replay word's PC+4, or the current\nrequest address when the last mapped word parks or a correction waits\nfor imemReady. Hold the candidates and selector when the producer does\nnot step. Reset to the fall-through candidate at PC zero. Keep the\nexisting common high-page register and full-width wraparound.\n\nSelect the ordinary producer address from the two registers before\napplying the existing registered EX recovery override. Feed the\nselected address to the direction hash, replay tag match, and PC+8\nlookup. Keep the common window and last-mapped-word flags synchronized\nwith the selected PC by updating them on the original producer\nhandshake. Preserve accepted-bus priority, empty-queue bypass,\nheld bus address, stale-response discard, last-word parking, and\nFENCE.I invalidation. Preserve the issued instruction's PC,\nprediction, and boundary marker through the queue and ordered\nsingle-channel retirement.\n\nThe scratch prototype reached 91.270, 90.518, and 90.518 MHz across\nthe three Gowin placements. It reproduced 3,558,019 timed cycles\nwith canonical CRCs and passed ready and stalled RVFI cosimulation.\nThat median implies 254.41 iterations per second, about 0.6% above the\nchampion. The longest path in the median placements moved to the\nqueue prediction bit, with forwarded ALU timing close behind.\nSeparately banking the boundary flag lowered placement-1 Fmax to\n88.860 MHz. The measured gain is below the acceptance margin,\nwhich requires a median above 94.12 MHz at this cycle count.\nRecheck all scored placements and the unmodified single-retire\nformal gate on\n…[9535 of 12607 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:b64061f514177d38]…\nnormally at single retirement width. Recovery discards the pair\nand younger queue state, including after a wrong prediction in either\nword. Reset and advancing FENCE.I clear the extra valid state as well\nas the existing replay state and cancel in-flight replay publication.\n\nA scratch prototype with pairing behind zero to three queued words\ncompleted canonical stalled CoreMark in 3,464,124 timed cycles, down\n2.64%. A simpler empty-queue-only prototype reached 83.848 MHz median\nwith queue feedback among its worst paths. Timing of the proposed\npaired admission with independent source matches is unmeasured. At\n3,464,124 cycles the median must exceed 91.64 MHz to clear the 4.6%\nthreshold. The 92.1 MHz target would give about 265.87 iterations/sec.\nCheck all three Gowin placements, canonical CRCs and the unchanged\nRVFI and formal gates. Exercise pairing with a resident older head,\nsimultaneous issue and refill, a full queue, both directions in the\nsecond word, wrong-path stores, a stale bus response and FENCE.I.\n \n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
