{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_44","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"rg '\\\"id\\\"\\\\s*:\\\\s*\\\"hyp-20261122-001-r13s0\\\"' cores/bench/experiments/log.jsonl | python3 -c 'import json,sys; r=json.load(sys.stdin); print(r[\\\"hypothesis\\\"][\\\"hypothesis\\\"])'\"","aggregated_output":"Add a restricted MEM-to-EX load bypass. Let a legal BEQ/BNE with a source\nmatching the in-flight load issue without a bubble. Also admit a legal\nload with a matching base, an unsigned two-bit byte offset, and an LW\nproducer. Register per-source matches with the consumer and retain its\nordinary forwarded operands for fallback. Use the bypass only when the\nproducer returns and writes its destination. A stalled bus holds both\ninstructions, and a misaligned producer leaves the consumer using its\nsaved fallback. Other consumers keep the raw-source interlock.\n\nFeed a dependent load's address from the raw LW word. Add the two low\nbits and propagate the carry to short upper groups in parallel, with a\nseparate input to the address register to avoid the general ALU path.\nKeep normal alignment checks and RVFI reporting for the complete address.\nFor equality branches, compare raw byte lanes with the other operand and\ncheck its required sign or zero extension in parallel. Capture partial\nequality and prequalified correction candidates on the EX/MEM edge. When\nthe reduced result calls for a correction, squash both younger instructions\nand register the selected recovery request before it drives fetch. Carry\nits window, boundary and PC+4 metadata alongside the address. Predict the\nfirst corrected word sequentially to keep the new recovery select off the\nordinary predictor and target arithmetic. Preserve stalled request\nretention, last mapped word parking, and FENCE.I. Hold a correcting late\nbranch's retirement for the extra recovery cycle so the existing liveness\nbound also covers a divide at the corrected PC. Keep ordinary training at\nthe EX edge when uncontested. Give an older late branch priority on a\ncollision and retain the younger update in a one-entry buffer. Suppress\ntraining for squashed or trapping branches.\n\nA scratch build with the extra recovery register completed in 3,387,761\ncycles. That count requires a median above 89.62 MHz for the >4.6%\nacceptance margin. Placement option 1 reached 79.621 MHz, limited by the\nshared recovery select through ordinary prediction and by ordinary EX\nbranch recovery. The proposed separate registered correction and PC+4\nmetadata target the first path. The ordinary EX path can still cap the\nscore, so the estimated fitness gain is low confidence.\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
