eader PC and\ninstruction. Match the normal PC register against the directory in\nparallel with the bus fetch and preselect the lowest PC match on a tie.\nCheck that entry's instruction encoding only to authorize the handshake.\nUse the ordinary bus path for the first corrected fetch. Each entry\nkeeps record 1, the first instruction after the header, in flops. Load it\ninto the shared replay output register on entry. Pre-read the following\nrecord from RAM using the directory match, then qualify the result with\nthe entry handshake. The next replay cycle can supply record 1 to the\nexisting five-entry fall-through queue. The\n…[12462 of 15534 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:e1e055672bfcafb7]…\nvalid state as well\nas the existing replay state and cancel in-flight replay publication.\n\nA scratch prototype with pairing behind zero to three queued words\ncompleted canonical stalled CoreMark in 3,464,124 timed cycles, down\n2.64%. A simpler empty-queue-only prototype reached 83.848 MHz median\nwith queue feedback among its worst paths. Timing of the proposed\npaired admission with independent source matches is unmeasured. At\n3,464,124 cycles the median must exceed 91.64 MHz to clear the 4.6%\nthreshold. The 92.1 MHz target would give about 265.87 iterations/sec.\nCheck all three Gowin placements, canonical CRCs and the unchanged\nRVFI and formal gates. Exercise pairing with a resident older head,\nsimultaneous issue and refill, a full queue, both directions in the\nsecond word, wrong-path stores, a stale bus response and FENCE.I.\n\n\nNone\n   text\t   data\t    bss\t    dec\t    hex\tfilename\n  16760\t     24\t     16\t  16800\t   41a0\t/srv/hwebench/tmp/58928045/c1c21728/bench-r15s1.Sq5L69/sliced/bench/programs/coremark.elf\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
