abled. Its Fmax was measured\\non the older combinational-divider core. The iterative-divider champion\\nreaches 48.196 MHz, and the other divider trial exposed an EX-to-fetch\\ntiming path. Preserving that clock while removing taken-transfer bubbles\\nis the opportunity for this predictor.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 7, \"confidence\": \"medium\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/core_pkg.sv\", \"description\": \"Carry the fetch incrementer result alongside the instruction into ID/EX for EX recovery and the jump link va\n…[10140 of 13212 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:168c2277ac37cbc0]…\ncted direct targets\", \"category\": \"predictor\", \"motivation\": \"The champion's four replay slots are filled from a synchronous PC+8 lookup. A predicted taken branch or JAL leaves that sequential stream, so either of the first two destination words can stall on imem while the replay slots catch up. A scratch 32-entry asynchronous target buffer saved 98,048 of 3,558,019 timed cycles, but the lookup and next-PC feedback reduced median Gowin Fmax to 85.508 MHz.\\n\", \"expected_impact\": {\"fitness_delta_pct\": 5, \"confidence\": \"low\"}, \"changes\": [{\"file\": \"rtl/if_stage.sv\", \"description\": \"Track the first two positions after a taken direct prediction and stage tagged fills into parity banks. Register the pre-read target pair, qualify it by producer PC and share the existing replay enqueue. Use the registered producer for the dynamic B/J lookup and predict sequentially on the first recovered bus word. Preserve full-queue backpressure, recovery, stale responses and boundary parking.\"}, {\"file\": \"test/test_pipeline.py\", \"\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
