 the last mapped word. Abort on an out-of-range PC or successor,\\nan early exit, or more than 128 records. Publish the entry only after the\\nfinal write. Each record contains the instruction, 18-bit word PC, 18-bit\\nresolved successor word PC and direct-taken bit. The terminal successor\\nis the header. Warm entries remain available across loop exits.\\n\\nEnter replay on ordinary bus acceptance of a matching header PC and\\ninstruction. Match the normal PC register against the directory in\\nparallel with the bus fetch and preselect the lowest PC match on a tie.\\nCheck that entry's instruction encoding only\n…[22438 of 25510 chars elided by tools/bench/transcript.py; sha256:643add356da2aea4]…\nll queue, both directions in the\\nsecond word, wrong-path stores, a stale bus response and FENCE.I.\\n\", 'expected_impact': {'fitness_delta_pct': 5, 'confidence': 'low'}, 'changes': [{'file': 'rtl/if_stage.sv', 'description': \"Co-admit a verified sequential follower from the existing PC+8 RAM and track its logical position in the five-word queue. Register the follower's head eligibility and select raw load-use matches before the payload mux.\"}, {'file': 'rtl/core.sv', 'description': \"Route the EX load destination and fetch's selected raw source match to the interlock while retaining the existing stall and squash policy.\"}, {'file': 'rtl/hazard_unit.sv', 'description': 'Use the fetch-selected raw source match as the alias input and retain existing valid, nonzero destination and load qualifications.'}, {'file': 'test/test_pipeline.py', 'description': 'Check paired fetch order, capacity, held paired heads, branch correction, stale acknowledgments and FENCE.I with ordered RVFI and no wrong-path stores.'}]}\n\nNone\n\n", "exit_code": 0, "status": "completed"}}
